eparate subdomains for gateway and dashboard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Rose <sella-media-hq@Mac.fritz.box>","tree":{"sha":"74a2ed4a5dc004ce5bee81542e09fd7bbfa6754e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WYJade/Agent-123/git/trees/74a2ed4a5dc004ce5bee81542e09fd7bbfa6754e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WYJade/Agent-123/git/commits/7233282f613e836058f4777040074a2e17bf223c","verification":{"payload":"tree 74a2ed4a5dc004ce5bee81542e09fd7bbfa6754e\nparent 980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7\nauthor YoungSella <155443947+YoungSella@users.noreply.github.com> 1778127591 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778127591 +0700\n\nfeat(docker): expose NEXT_PUBLIC_* as build args (#643)\n\nBrowser-side env vars must be baked at Next.js build time. Adding ARG/ENV pairs in the build stage allows operators to configure the gateway URL via docker build --build-arg or compose.yml args without forking the image. Backward-compatible: defaults remain empty, behaviour unchanged when no build args are passed. Discovered via Project EIGHTBALL deployment with separate subdomains for gateway and dashboard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Rose <sella-media-hq@Mac.fritz.box>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BLnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9bkQAEhPimLS5F9g/us7eu/ChHs7\nVTCEqn8Qv2UD9WBezGgkumHnaHPg+XSuZefmVghL8F6oDTD67w9ULH7F8nuN/dyk\nEUcCvG6OAF2fJBPVrjXV6xCvQ3VziVjG8t1gLRDQgDcMBukCZ94dMccLZUtYg8EN\n3VfgvGKCWLLbN6zC5n7EwVpIZUvxw2M2KihFhf7TA6GxW8DVZn2pyPb9SYfOL/IQ\nfhfSs2N7Ir52jkK4/OWZO54LgSqVSvhCjRpnFBSwpQ/zAKaroTp0p5IZ18zbf28z\nGjN64R68q2SoUlfk+M3fbiy80KcfuCoo2Te5airXVdeofdvHze1P0l/UU+yfzPvt\nGixFEy72ztfnl8V/ErMYpbinF/YW1AxNDzAt8FaG+U8nR4S+ipU3vOQQco2WlsX8\nefh6rNGh/HsT64abuVSST9KDi9AzEKMcxWaj+V3eOhtf51f+UBHP3bJlF0M7VcwH\nrQDmeTH84ovuYCzu3RMLjEkc7it2vosifEMQAVrqOBZFHu0yPaHlqTM48q1eP8fI\ntrUh/YZyrwbrjGBZBxs9AxcJk4cquq+TQ3gApRZN0u8/oUvp5YatQAGCNS7rsgYd\nAmhpXvF1rk1a7qWja0/AvfZCx6G0kxue40hw0RMopPkO7lQpySp95U5A6YUKc07y\nP+V3PQ2EJEvrdFWS560T\n=GN6+\n----