bution work must remain fully isolated under /Users/ravi/Code/forks\nRejected: Manually create test-results or rely on ambient lockfile layout | brittle and not reproducible\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep verification tooling self-contained in the fork workspace; do not reintroduce assumptions about parent-directory state\nTested: pnpm build; pnpm lint from a clean state\nNot-tested: Alternate package-manager layouts beyond the current pnpm-based workspace\n\n* Document OpenCode session API semantics clearly\n\nUpdate the OpenAPI contract so the expanded runtime/session surface describes\nOpenCode accurately, including transcript and continue behavior plus honest\n500-path error semantics for continue when the local runtime cannot satisfy a\nsaved session.\n\nConstraint: Contract parity must stay green while describing behavior truthfully\nRejected: Leave continue/transcript behavior implicit | would make the docs disagree with tested runtime behavior\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep the OpenAPI spec aligned with route behavior whenever OpenCode session semantics evolve\nTested: pnpm api:parity\nNot-tested: External client generation against the updated schema\n\n* Document OpenCode capabilities in the API index\n\nUpdate the route catalog copy so the public API index reflects the actual\nsession capabilities after native OpenCode support, including transcript and\ncontinue coverage without implying unsupported PTY behavior.\n\nConstraint: The API index must stay truthful without broadening scope beyond the implemented OpenCode paths\nRejected: Leave the catalog at Claude/Codex wording | would under-document the shipped OpenCode surface\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nDirective: Keep the API index descriptions aligned with the OpenAPI contract and actual route behavior\nTested: pnpm api:parity\nNot-tested: Downstream docs consumers beyond the built-in API index view\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ravi Tharuma <RaviTharuma@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3nSwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMhsQAAz7qls7qLe3wSWKCTp+kUcy\nHTtekD1H7rWK/0QNpcUIlubfVzcXxbrVZltImmDlPTj5x1HgQ5FxMiavyEpYwD66\najKUQejSMYAkqcHemIgbwriRVAMYVWAEnKyTLJMDDN8MdooQB6Nxrcc1pzIcvt0E\nLuR+5t6o0cc1UFmMvJE3Q2p4Vo1YAookbzMhaZYedfS5C4se6bmf7y5Nj88S1Hlh\noIBrYF1N0BPck4ClwnAuCVvL8kM4WSBdg75oKlKiJi2MIDhQwoMtEfd2yyskWwj/\n7eYBvRb4xU5/X353tq4cuWNgplBkTmSG2ojLjtbgydZvyDEABiaWlSKVKa82pFC1\nViedAjS3GLC692YuOtDy+O3v1Q/3h9GSKaBC4DKjyFlaROplB381tzF3gxgK0SbW\nQhumrEqSaP0WgQsLdKX0KoUEP/Ix+u98kHbAKNqHlHdw49aH0pp3tDzobhmquzEu\nWv6aZeZVQzM2yRJ88vWCg7YS2G8cS5kgfW05ULGTYsIcZUVPmTBwz+w1DeWvbCcW\nwojY6yYO1o+rUll7BfQ8oLFt5C/f+ZPoM+aqGEuB0/FD0Q7ScLdyVp9X9Y76/waB\nVtvkkogp69DHnzW1nqivUalmyMwi64wi0xolSq/Cgf9c7EEg/2M6sXZOgVxtbB4C\nfHDiYnEKA68KLFYvrFRH\n=B4H0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T10:42:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/WYJade/Agent-123/commit/90a5615fc73dc03e35c1dc886bc6468013eb2275","node_id":"C_kwD