","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fujivara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fujivara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fujivara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fujivara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fujivara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fujivara/notifly/commits/e8001f363210d080874e6da6e31fd60182ac700a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-26T14:49:12Z","email":"marat.skyba@gmail.com","name":"Marat Skyba"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-26T14:49:12Z","email":"marat.skyba@gmail.com","name":"Marat Skyba"},"message":"feat: delete account (cascade flows + revoke auth)\n\n- settings.page: confirmDeleteAccount() shows an Ionic AlertController dialog\n  with destructive role (Cancel / Delete). On confirm, performDeleteAccount:\n    1. Lists the user''s templates\n    2. For each, disarms its runtime triggers (best-effort; runtime is\n       optional so no-op on web) then deletes via repository.delete\n    3. Calls AuthService.deleteCurrentUser to remove the Firebase account\n    4. Navigates to /onboarding\n- Lifts the Delete account row out of demo-settings into the live Data\n  section (sits next to Export, styled with settings__row--danger).\n- Note: orphaned ProcessExecution rows and the User DC record aren''t\n  explicitly deleted here. They lose their access path with auth removed.\n  Server-side cleanup (Cloud Function on auth.user.delete) is the proper\n  follow-up for full GDPR erasure.","tree":{"sha":"968452a8fe67f6ea924937d523072ab24c515ee0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fujivara/notifly/git/trees/968452a8fe67f6ea924937d523072ab24c515ee0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fujivara/notifly/git/commits/e8001f363210d080874e6da6e31fd60182ac700a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verif