k-sizing math; swap lockfile Q for dependency confusion\n\nThe disk example now genuinely diverges (800 MB/s peak path 484 TB vs\n200 MB/s x RF3 363 TB); the lockfile question restating its own pitfall\nbecomes the dependency-confusion attack question.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0373f05c84b8aef1b7fc34371b9d3663a1aae884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/0373f05c84b8aef1b7fc34371b9d3663a1aae884"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/389d54ae1c5e18f5be516b96119738011cca44d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/389d54ae1c5e18f5be516b96119738011cca44d1","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDM4OWQ1NGFlMWM1ZTE4ZjViZTUxNmI5NjExOTczODAxMWNjYTQ0ZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a","sha":"2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a"}],"sha":"389d54ae1c5e18f5be516b96119738011cca44d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/389d54ae1c5e18f5be516b96119738011cca44d1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T07:35:08Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T07:35:08Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(fastapi): replace duplicated consumer-shutdown question; correct httpx auth_flow claim\n\nQ16 becomes the ungraceful-exit rebalance-stall question (session.timeout.ms\nvs max.poll.interval.ms); the auth_flow answer now states the truth — await\nin a sync generator is a SyntaxError, not a silent no-op.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5ded7004b63782a519600a52097215afbcc3f26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/e5ded7004b63782a519600a52097215afbcc3f26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDJlYmMyMjhhMjc1YTUzODdjZTQ3ZjFkNzI1OTdjY2YzNWMyMDZlNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/f2ab3131992e2ea00ab8882816ed23cdd5cb1266","sha":"f2ab3131992e2ea00ab8882816ed23cdd5cb1266","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/f2ab3131992e2ea00ab8882816ed23cdd5cb1266"}],"sha":"2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2ebc228a275a5387ce47f1d72597ccf35c206e5a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/f2ab3131992e2ea00ab8882816ed23cdd5cb1266/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T07:32:44Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T07:32:44Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(backend,hld): correct burn-rate math, Shenandoah JDK version, Bazel timeout; replace two cross-section overlaps\n\n100x burn on a 28-day budget exhausts in ~6.7 hours, not 24 minutes;\nShenandoah went production in JDK 15 (JEP 379); Bazel large tests default\nto a 900s timeout; the two migration questions overlapping the database\nsibling become ddl-auto risk and cross-service schema coordination.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1adc55795d8b1ee9349775ac2a330928896ddd6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/1adc55795