 96px clearance.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b37d4c3ac2b07674d1c8acd915d0284dc412c660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/b37d4c3ac2b07674d1c8acd915d0284dc412c660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0f6430db43ee06f5772b45c132cea1fdd0b7a149","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0f6430db43ee06f5772b45c132cea1fdd0b7a149","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBmNjQzMGRiNDNlZTA2ZjU3NzJiNDVjMTMyY2VhMWZkZDBiN2ExNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c","sha":"4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c"}],"sha":"0f6430db43ee06f5772b45c132cea1fdd0b7a149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0f6430db43ee06f5772b45c132cea1fdd0b7a149"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:24:51Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T15:24:51Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"Reader Updates","tree":{"sha":"a7615b07dadd75231c41368b20cfaf012506ae04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/a7615b07dadd75231c41368b20cfaf012506ae04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDRlNWU2NmM0YWI0YWNmZTJkMjk4MjQ2ZWIxYjM3MTVjYTFhMWFmOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a","sha":"65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a"}],"sha":"4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4e5e66c4ab4acfe2d298246eb1b3715ca1a1af9c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:45:22Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:45:22Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): immersive reading mode + reader delight (callouts, scroll-spy, find, typography, haptics)\n\nMake the study reader beautiful and non-boring, on desktop and phone. All within\nthe reader''s hard invariants (pitch-black bg, pure-white prose; colour lives only\nin bordered \"dark islands\"). No content or extract.py change.\n\nImmersive reading mode (F / ⛶ / Exit pill):\n- Extends applyReaderModes into setReaderFull(): hides topbar + mobile tab bar +\n  auto-hides the reader toolbar; centres a measure-capped column. Head reveals on\n  top-edge hover (desktop) or a tap on the peek strip (touch); a floating Exit\n  pill is the always-there control. Safe-area insets for notches/home indicators.\n- Layers the native Fullscreen API on top (requestFullscreen on #reader, webkit\n  fallback), with graceful degrade to in-app immersive when the browser blocks it;\n  a fullscreenchange listener keeps state in sync on OS/Esc exit.\n\nReader richness:\n- Callout blocks: blockquotes promoted to Note/Tip/Warning/Key-Insight/War-Story\n  islands when the first line is a GFM alert (> [!NOTE]) or a known bold label\n  (> **Warning:**). Plain quotes are untouched. (calloutOf unit-tested, 8/8.)\n- Scroll-spy TOC (active-section highlight + \"§X / M\"), \"~N min read · M sections\"\n  chip, and per-path scroll-position memory (revisits resume where you left off).\n- In-page find: Ctrl/Cmd+F inside the reader (not the global palette), text-node-\n  safe <mark> highlighting with next/prev + count; Esc/close restores the DOM.\n- Typography popover (Aa): serif toggle, measure presets (narrow/cozy/wide/auto),\n  drop-cap. Applied on <html> so prefs persist across navigations; colour untouched.\n\nDelight:\n- Haptics: navigator.vibrate paired with the same beats as sfx (correct/wrong/\n  combo + celebratory moments), gated on coarse pointer + sound-mute + reduced-motion.\n- Reading feeds the game: mark a module read on >=90% scroll (or dwell), additive\n  sd_progress fields (readModules + a daily reading tracker w/ its own streak);\n  ✓ ticks in the module tree + a \"N read today\" chip on Home. Blitz XP untouched.\n\nVerified: node --check clean; app boots to Home with no console errors; callout\ndetection unit-tested. Interactive reader rendering not visually verified this\nsession (Chrome extension disconnected; headless deep-link can''t drive the SPA).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0c5f1082ca61fce0a5b9f5148ed334d91c767786","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/0c5f1082ca61fce0a5b9f5148ed334d91c767786"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDY1ZGMzNTk3NjlmODY3NDA1NDk1NWU2ZGFhYTdkMDBiZDc4ZTNhNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96","sha":"9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96"}],"sha":"65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/65dc359769f8674054955e6daaa7d00bd78e3a4a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:00:56Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:00:56Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): wrap code blocks on mobile for readable study content\n\nThe reader trapped long code lines behind a horizontal scroll, so on a\nphone you read source one line-fragment at a time. Three scoped fixes:\n\n- <=640px: `pre code:not(.diagram)` wraps (pre-wrap + overflow-wrap:\n  anywhere). ASCII diagrams (.diagram) stay `white-space: pre` so their\n  monospace column alignment (causal masks, box-drawing) is preserved.\n- Inline `code` gets overflow-wrap so long tokens break instead of\n  forcing the whole page into horizontal scroll on narrow screens.\n- Copy button revealed under `@media (hover: none)` — it was opacity:0\n  and hover-only, i.e. permanently invisible on touch devices.\n\nCSS-only (game reader surface); no content or extract.py change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"59079ed333e40b68327417532d4f0002c3996595","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/59079ed333e40b68327417532d4f0002c3996595"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDlkYjk1ZmRjODAxN2EwZmFlZTRiZTE4ZjM1YWI5NjIwMzJmNmZkOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2","sha":"1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2"}],"sha":"9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9db95fdc8017a0faee4be18f35ab962032f6fd96"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:05:16Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:05:16Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs(mermaid skill): add render-check gotchas from the diagram rollout\n\nAdd five gotchas the rollout''s mmdc render pass surfaced (structural linting is\nblind to non-flowchart syntax): semicolons as statement separators in sequenceDiagram\nNotes; reserved-keyword ids (rect/graph/end, $ in classDiagram ids); colons in\nquadrantChart labels; classDiagram tilde-generics and the no-classDef rule for\nclass/sequence/state diagrams; and the render-to-verify step itself (caught 6 real\nparse errors the linter and authoring agents missed across the lld/case-study waves).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d307374460432df5df4f34c09718fa4a5289d65e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/d307374460432df5df4f34c09718fa4a5289d65e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDFlY2VkYjJiMWI3OTFjN2Y3ZWNhYTNiOTIzMTMyYjNlMmQ0MGFjYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/561cb9179fe85b32203be4da238f58cfe9523767","sha":"561cb9179fe85b32203be4da238f58cfe9523767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/561cb9179fe85b32203be4da238f58cfe9523767"}],"sha":"1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1ecedb2b1b791c7f7ecaa3b923132b3e2d40aca2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/561cb9179fe85b32203be4da238f58cfe9523767/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:03:50Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:03:50Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs(book,cs_fundamentals): sync CLAUDE.md diagram rule to appeal-first policy\n\nBoth section CLAUDE.md files still declared \"ASCII diagrams only — no Mermaid\",\nstale vs the 2026-07-02 appeal-first policy in root CLAUDE.md and now contradicted\nby the committed Mermaid rollout (book chapters + cs_fundamentals modules and\ndsa_patterns files all carry Mermaid). Update the four blanket prohibitions to\n\"appeal-first: Mermaid preferred for topological diagrams; ASCII kept for grids/\nbyte-layouts/geometry\". Visual Intuition Diagram sections (ASCII-specific\narchetypes) left as-is, deferring to root for the full policy. Flagged repeatedly\nby rollout agents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef0f6d7d53b0f53bd9b6bd82f5400464cfcec378","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/ef0f6d7d53b0f53bd9b6bd82f5400464cfcec378"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/561cb9179fe85b32203be4da238f58cfe9523767","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url"