system-design/commit/bb296f1070ed76937a7ae184121760813e30fe84","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGJiMjk2ZjEwNzBlZDc2OTM3YTdhZTE4NDEyMTc2MDgxM2UzMGZlODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f","sha":"4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f"}],"sha":"bb296f1070ed76937a7ae184121760813e30fe84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bb296f1070ed76937a7ae184121760813e30fe84"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T15:36:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T15:36:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): brand logo click returns to home\n\nCompletes the guarded #brandHome handler that landed in d88c263 (pauses a live\nblitz before navigating): adds the id + ARIA button role to the brand element\nand the pointer cursor / focus-visible outline styling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2b46f362e6054073cc79502117aa4c7dbc5d0e41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/2b46f362e6054073cc79502117aa4c7dbc5d0e41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDRhMTAxYTA2YzFjMGQ2MTY3ZDkyNmM5MjM4ZTYwNGY0ZjdhZmM5NmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36","sha":"af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36"}],"sha":"4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4a101a06c1c0d6167d926c9238e604f4f7afc96f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T15:18:14Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T15:18:14Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(hld,database): convert ASCII diagrams to colored Mermaid + net-new (diagram wave 1a)\n\nInterview-path modules in hld and database had zero Mermaid. Converted 175\ntopological ASCII diagrams to colored One-Dark Mermaid (flowchart/sequence/state/\nxychart/quadrant/pie/timeline) and added 58 net-new for mechanics trapped in prose.\nKept 102 ASCII blocks Mermaid cannot draw (constraint grids, hash-ring geometry,\nvalue tables).\n\n- 247 mermaid blocks across 30 module READMEs (incl. the hld/caching pilot)\n- all 156 flowcharts fully classed with the One-Dark palette; classDef ordering\n  and bracket-trap lint clean; agents render-validated most files with\n  mermaid-cli 11.16.0 (the reader''s CDN version)\n- also fixes hld/message_queues cross-link after the FastAPI section move\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac8d65054278b96305e219b642cc3a3e20cbf82c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/ac8d65054278b96305e219b642cc3a3e20cbf82c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGFmMjNhYWI3MzI1MWU3NzhlZmUxYzMxODI3MjAxNDA5M2E3NTlkMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821","sha":"d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821"}],"sha":"af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/af23aab73251e778efe1c318272014093a759d36"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:47:02Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T14:47:02Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"refactor(fastapi): split FastAPI into its own top-level section\n\nMove python/fastapi/ -> fastapi/ as a peer section of Python. FastAPI is now\n19 modules + 6 case studies; Python is 21 pure-Python modules.\n\n- git mv preserves history for the 18 unchanged module dirs\n- deterministic relative-link fixes in moved files; reverse-link repaths in\n  python/README (59) and root README (26)\n- game wiring (app.js): SECTION_LABELS + STUDY_ORDER split (python 21 / new\n  fastapi 19, adjacent in the picker) + STUDY_PATHS split (interview 13 / 9)\n- section docs: new fastapi/README.md (section index) + fastapi/CLAUDE.md;\n  python/README + python/CLAUDE rescoped to pure Python (also fixed 8\n  pre-existing ../../ cross-links)\n- root README/CLAUDE: FastAPI added as a peer section\n\nDeferred: hld/message_queues has 2 python/fastapi links, fixed with the diagram\nwave (that file is being diagram-edited concurrently). Bank + graphs regenerate\nin CI on push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9921f47481a3655de707613a3edd3443b5341a4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/9921f47481a3655de707613a3edd3443b5341a4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGQ4OGMyNjNhZTAxZjRlYzY1NjUzMmU2MzkyOTc3NDdlZmM4MGE4MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f","sha":"0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f"}],"sha":"d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d88c263ae01f4ec656532e639297747efc80a821"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:51:29Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:51:29Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs(cuda): prefix module Q&As with Q: and codify the convention\n\nThe CUDA section was authored after the repo-wide Q: normalization (ae92f65),\nso its §12 interview questions rendered without the **Q: label every other\nsection uses. Prefix all 410 module Q&As across 23 modules to match the\nLLM-section convention (extract.py strips the label, so the MCQ bank is\nunchanged). CUDA case-study §11 Q&As already carried the prefix — untouched.\n\nAlso codify the convention so future sections don''t miss it:\n- root CLAUDE.md -> Interview Q&A Rules: mandate **Q: <question>?**\n- cuda/CLAUDE.md -> Adding a New CUDA Module step 1\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c245703de313ded2b025944434c19960f1eaff72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/c245703de313ded2b025944434c19960f1eaff72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBiYjRkOWIzNzNlMzQxOWFmMTZiMjVhYWQ2ZGZjMTI1NDU1YTI2M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac","sha":"484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac"}],"sha":"0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0bb4d9b373e3419af16b25aad6dfc125455a263f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:50:10Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:50:10Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game/reader): render indented code fences and wrapped/renumbered lists\n\nThe Markdown reader is line-based and only recognized blocks starting at\ncolumn 0, so any fenced code block or list content indented under a list\nmarker fell through to inline/paragraph handling. Three symptoms, one cause:\n\n- §10/§14 BROKEN->FIX code fences (indented 3 spaces inside a numbered list)\n  rendered as flowing prose with collapsed newlines and leaked ``` backticks.\n- Wrapped list items lost their continuation lines, so each became its own\n  single-item <ol> — and a standalone <ol> always restarts at 1, making every\n  discussion question and §10 pitfall display \"1.\".\n\nFixes in mdRender():\n- Fence opener is now indent-tolerant; the opener''s indent is stripped from\n  the body (relative indentation preserved). The closing fence must be\n  indented no more than the opener, so an ASCII diagram that legitimately\n  *shows* indented ```lang fences (autogen.md, design_ai_code_review.md) is\n  never split early — column-0 openers behave exactly as before.\n- List parser absorbs indented continuation lines into the current <li> and\n  emits <ol start=\"N\"> so a list resuming after an interrupting code block\n  continues its numbering.\n\nVerified across all 832 md files: 0 render exceptions, 0 unbalanced list tags;\n32 previously-broken indented fences now render; the 2 at-risk diagram blocks\nstay intact. Rendering-only, no extract.py impact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ece38264c1a27dcd08e2c07abe456777a60764eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/ece38264c1a27dcd08e2c07abe456777a60764eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDQ4NDM3NmMwMDY0YjQ5OTc2N2ZiZWYzMWE1YTZiOGU5NjI1OWMxYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621","sha":"d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621"}],"sha":"484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/484376c0064b499767fbef31a5a6b8e96259c1ac"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:30:43Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:30:43Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game/reader): syntax-highlight C/C++/CUDA/PTX code fences\n\nThe reader''s hand-rolled tokenizer only colored fences whose language\ntag was in LANG_DEFS (java/js/python/sql/yaml/bash/json/…). cpp, cuda,\nc, and ptx fences fell through to verbatim white — visible in the CUDA\nsection where 168 cpp + 82 cuda blocks rendered uncolored while the\nPython/bash blocks in the same files highlighted normally.\n\nAdd a cpp LANG_DEFS entry (C/C++/CUDA keywords incl. __global__/__device__/\n__shared__ qualifiers, built-in + CUDA vector types, threadIdx/blockIdx/\nblockDim/gridDim/warpSize) and alias cuda/cu/cuh/c/cc/cxx/c++/h/hpp/ptx\nto it. Table-driven, so the fix applies repo-wide. Rendering-only — no\nextract.py re-run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0947fe2748227fa375891064cf1ef69e4da3ab78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/0947fe2748227fa375891064cf1ef69e4da3ab78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGQ5YzY4MzQzNjMyNjEzNmI1MjdhMmY0YmU5NmVlNzI3ODcyZmU2MjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510","sha":"f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510"}],"sha":"d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d9c683436326136b527a2f4be96ee727872fe621"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:15:16Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:15:16Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Full/Interview study paths across all sections + 20 gap modules + diagram rules\n\nInterview-Specific learning path rolled out to every game section except book: a STUDY_PATHS[section].interview subset in app.js plus a README ''Learning Paths'' + ''Knowledge-Question Map'' + ''Study Plan'' block and a CLAUDE.md sync note per section. All 12 interview arrays validated as forward-ordered subsets of STUDY_ORDER (ordered=true, 0 missing).\n\nNew gap modules (14-section template, 15+ Q&As each): ml (imbalanced_data_and_leakage_traps, information_retrieval_and_search, speech_and_audio_ml, meta_learning_and_few_shot, fairness_and_responsible_ai); java (json_processing_jackson, logging, java_platform_module_system, reference_types_and_cleaners, graalvm_native_image, build_tools_maven_gradle); spring (spring_data_nosql, database_migrations, spring_websocket_stomp, spring_http_clients); cs_fundamentals (theory_of_computation, how_code_runs_compilers_and_interpreters, discrete_math_for_engineers, character_encoding_deep_dive); llm (byte_level_and_tokenizer_free sub-file).\n\nDiagram authoring rules added to CLAUDE.md, the /mermaid-diagrams skill, and game/README.md: colour every node, horizontal-first (flowchart LR), no spillover text, rounded corners. Corrected the reader colouring contract to match the code — mmTintPlain tints only unstyled nodes (authored colours always win), degrading per-node rather than bailing to flat grey.\n\nAlso registers the cuda section in the game (STUDY_ORDER.cuda, STUDY_PATHS.cuda.interview, root tables); cuda content is in the companion commit 8fb5461.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"740c1dbd670bccc2b2deb85bac2d4745f059b30e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/740c1dbd670bccc2b2deb85bac2d4745f059b30e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGYyZjFmYjJiNDhjYjUyNGE4MmViZjViMDY3NDAzODg1ZjEwMTI1MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4","sha":"8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4"}],"sha":"f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/f2f1fb2b48cb524a82ebf5b067403885f1012510"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:14:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T13:14:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(cuda): add GPGPU/CUDA section — 24 modules, 6 case studies\n\nKernel-author''s guide to CUDA/GPGPU across 6 phases: the SIMT model and GPU hardware, core CUDA programming, the performance-engineering discipline (coalescing, shared-memory tiling, occupancy, warp primitives), advanced execution (streams, graphs, multi-GPU/NCCL), the library + Tensor-Core ecosystem, and the profiling/debugging/portability toolchain. Dual CUDA C++ + Python (CuPy/Numba/Triton/PyTorch). Includes the section knowledge graph (game/graph/cuda.json).\n\nGame wiring (STUDY_ORDER/STUDY_PATHS, root tables) rides in the companion learning-paths commit, which shares app.js/README/CLAUDE.md with cross-section work.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5ba4ed3d9e643aacab3f3b96591f2df1a425816","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/a5ba4ed3d9e643aacab3f3b96591f2df1a425816"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDhmYjU0NjEwMTQ5MTA1YzQxOWYzYTljNzEzZGJlNTM4NDRjY2RkZDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88","sha":"0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88"}],"sha":"8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/8fb54610149105c419f3a9c713dbe53844ccddd4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T09:06:23Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T09:06:23Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game/llm): dual Full/Interview-Specific study paths (LLM pilot)\n\nAdd a curated 30-module Interview-Specific learning path alongside the\nfull 52-module curriculum. The game''s Study view gains a Full/Interview\nsegmented toggle; the LLM README documents both paths.\n\n- app.js: STUDY_PATHS const (per-section interview subsets, only llm now);\n  filter in openStudySection after modulesOf; getStudyPath/setStudyPath\n  helpers persist choice in sd_study_path (default full, section-gated).\n- style.css: .pathswitch/.pathopt mirroring the existing .lenbar control.\n- llm/README.md: new \"## Learning Paths\" section (Full + Interview 30).\n- game/CLAUDE.md, llm/CLAUDE.md: dual-source sync note (README<->STUDY_PATHS).\n\nVerified live: full=52 nodes, interview=30, persists across reload,\nsections without an interview path show no toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9e7098a1efca347b9914f1868bb6aca6912fe50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/e9e7098a1efca347b9914f1868bb6aca6912fe50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBmZDM5YzBjODBlZTk4OTIzODE5ZGExZDVmZTY4ZGJlMzMwNjRjODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8","sha":"ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8"}],"sha":"0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0fd39c0c80ee98923819da1d5fe68dbe33064c88"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T16:37:40Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T16:37:40Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs: prefix all interview questions with Q: for repo-wide consistency\n\nStandardize interview-question labeling across every section to match the\nLLM section''s **Q:** convention.\n\n- Adds **Q:** to unprefixed interview questions (was plain **question?**)\n- Converts numbered-list questions **N. ...** -> **QN:** (rescues the\n  non-\"?\" ones that extract.py previously dropped from the quiz bank)\n- Leaves existing **Q1:**/**Q:** labels untouched (additive only)\n- Scoped strictly to interview Q&A / discussion sections, so prose\n  emphasis and war-story list items are never touched\n\n272 files, 9,181 questions now carry a Q-prefix (0 unprefixed remaining).\nextract.py regenerates clean at 7,603 MCQs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73d857170daf697aa5b98e869ab94bc8edfac5be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/73d857170daf697aa5b98e869ab94bc8edfac5be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGFlOTJmNjU1ODhkMjFkNjRiZmVjNDMyZTFmOTBlNTVhOGMxNDc5Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90","sha":"09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90"}],"sha":"ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/ae92f65588d21d64bfec432e1f90e55a8c1479c8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T15:54:43Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T15:54:43Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game/reader): pure-white prose, mermaid text containment, universal rounding, fit-to-width\n\n- --rd-text #e6e6e6 -> #ffffff (owner-updated hard limit; game/CLAUDE.md revised)\n- sequence diagrams measured text in Open Sans/Trebuchet but displayed\n  monospace, so notes/actors were sized ~25% too narrow and dark text spilled\n  onto the black canvas: sequence.{actor,message,note}FontFamily now match\n  themeVariables.fontFamily, and any residual under-measured note/actor rect\n  is widened post-render to cover its own text (mermaid under-measures long\n  mono runs even with matched fonts)\n- round every rect >=12px tall in non-chart diagrams (actors, notes, frames,\n  timeline periods), not just flowchart .node rects; chart data marks exempt\n- new .mm-fit pill on overflowing (h-scroll) diagrams: scales the svg to the\n  live width between the sidebars, remembered per-container (data-mm-fit) and\n  re-applied by the ResizeObserver, which now also watches the sidebars since\n  collapsing one changes only the gutters without resizing the column\n- docs: mermaid skill gotchas + root CLAUDE.md post-processing paragraph +\n  generated-not-committed bank contract\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"22169deb9d0b11857e178d232ed8de933c96abca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/22169deb9d0b11857e178d232ed8de933c96abca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDA5OTQxMjUyYTI2NGExYjg2NTFhNDhiOGYxNjU2ZjVkMWIzNjVmOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e","sha":"176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e"}],"sha":"09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/09941252a264a1b8651a48b8f1656f5d1b365f90"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T15:54:42Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T15:54:42Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"chore(game): stop committing generated question banks\n\nquestions/*.json (~16MB) are extract.py output and the Pages workflow\nregenerates them fresh on every deploy (pages.yml has never needed the\ncommitted copies). Drop them from the repo and gitignore the path; run\nextract.py locally when playing off a local server.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb771803226698d74c3610d26cf14a6ee4ce5e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/eb771803226698d74c3610d26cf14a6ee4ce5e35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDE3NmQ0YTI0OGM5NWY4M2JjODkwNDA5OTMwYTE1NDY1YTdiNzIzNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c","sha":"86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c"}],"sha":"176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/176d4a248c95f83bc890409930a15465a7b7236e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T15:15:01Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T15:15:01Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game): four cross-phase defects from the full-diff code review\n\n- finishPrime left the stale pretest screen mounted under the reader; its\n  leftover Finish button could re-record the no-stakes pretest as a graded\n  session (XP/streak/SM-2 corruption). The study path now renders as the\n  real underlayer before the reader opens.\n- Boss-intro dismiss keys leaked through to the quiz handler and could lock\n  an answer on the just-revealed 2x boss question (stopImmediatePropagation).\n- Keys other than Escape now stop at an open pause sheet / help overlay\n  instead of grading the question hidden behind it.\n- onHashChange''s reader-close branch swallowed code-driven navigation\n  (palette/pause-and-leave jumps stranded users on a stale screen with a\n  mismatched hash); Back-to-underlayer still closes in place, any other\n  route now falls through to the guard + dispatch.\n\nVerified: B 26/26, A2 42/43 (known bank-data precondition), syntax clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5d54be1d8acb8c10aabe35048724346f518696c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/5d54be1d8acb8c10aabe35048724346f518696c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDg2YmI1NmE2OTRjZWMzMDI2MTc5YzIwZTM5Y2E1ZDk5NTJkNDkyOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada","sha":"75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada"}],"sha":"86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/86bb56a694cec3026179c20e39ca5d9952d4928c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T14:50:27Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T14:50:27Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): insights, command palette, mobile pass, beauty pass, docs (Phase E2)\n\n- Insights: Progress gains a memory forecast (14-day due chart), strongest/\n  shakiest modules with one-tap drills, leeches (lazy-loaded hardest\n  questions), per-section confidence calibration, 30-day XP+accuracy trend,\n  and a session log — all derived from existing localStorage state.\n- Cmd+K command palette: fuzzy jump across sections, ~340 modules\n  (read/quiz), verbs (resume, review, gauntlet, codex, themes), and cached-\n  bank question full-text search.\n- Mobile: bottom tab bar <640px, sticky quiz actions, Learning Path chords\n  hidden on touch, heatmap horizontal scroll, 44px targets.\n- Beauty: reveal choreography, directional question transitions, staggered\n  results, mastery-delta shine on Home tiles, view-transition slide-fade.\n- Docs: game README and CLAUDE.md rewritten for the Pages-only architecture\n  and the full feature set; root CLAUDE.md game row updated.\n\nVerified: 40/40 new checks + E1 regression, zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b80d103ac344d42e24ba9e152878199ff2593af6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/b80d103ac344d42e24ba9e152878199ff2593af6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDc1ZjRhZmZhZGQ4YWZmMzExOGFhYTk3NmM5MTMyMTYwNDQyZjBhZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659","sha":"d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659"}],"sha":"75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/75f4affadd8aff3118aaa976c9132160442f0ada"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T14:26:14Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T14:26:14Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(java,spring): visual-first Mermaid conversion + zero-gap expansion\n\nBring java/ and spring/ to visual-first parity with llm/ and ml/ — they\nwere the last sections on the pre-appeal-first ASCII diagram policy.\n\n- Diagrams: 0 -> 253 Mermaid fences (java 100, spring 153); appeal-first\n  conversion across module READMEs + case studies. Legit ASCII kept for\n  byte/heap-layout grids, propagation timelines, N+1 logs, capacity math.\n- New java modules: java_time_datetime, bytecode_and_classfile,\n  security_and_cryptography (+ regex/ReDoS and JMX deep-dive sub-files).\n- New spring modules: spring_hateoas_rest_maturity, spring_grpc,\n  spring_session (+ RSocket and i18n deep-dive sub-files).\n- Q&A: all elevated floors (18+) met and extractable; ordering\n  gotchas -> internals -> edge cases preserved.\n- Cross-links: java -> hld/cs_fundamentals and spring -> hld added\n  (were 0); ~40 inline See Also links; 4 broken relative links fixed.\n- Governance: both sub-CLAUDE.md \"Visual Intuition Diagrams\" sections\n  reconciled to the appeal-first Mermaid policy; master READMEs + module\n  tables + cross-reference maps updated for the new modules/sub-files.\n\nextract.py: trim an over-long Q&A first sentence at a clause boundary\ninstead of dropping the whole question, so questions are treated equally\nregardless of length (recovered ~1,086 questions repo-wide). Question\nbanks regenerate in CI on push.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27553ba7d10f7ecd57bf0a83de2fbfd991e07f16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/27553ba7d10f7ecd57bf0a83de2fbfd991e07f16"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGQ4ZmYyMTZlMGYwYjIyMDUzZTU0MTk1MDNlNjFiZjc4YzJiYWI2NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f","sha":"462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f"}],"sha":"d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d8ff216e0f0b22053e5419503e61bf78c2bab659"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T14:00:49Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T14:00:49Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game/reader): \"Evaluate me\" — one-click topic quiz at the end of every page\n\nEvery module page (and deep-dive sub-file) rendered in the reader now ends\nwith an Evaluate yourself block: live question count for that module, one\nbutton that closes the reader and starts a blitz scoped to exactly that\ntopic. Hidden mid-quiz and on non-module pages (section roots, case studies);\nbackground bank load warms the cache so the quiz starts instantly; skipped on\ndata-saver connections.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e24da69cfac96b4da09ff2eb17b32ef5a8ea94e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/e24da69cfac96b4da09ff2eb17b32ef5a8ea94e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDQ2MmNjZWUyMjY3YjY0MTQ2ODdjMTdmMDczZWM0ZGUxMmE2ZjJjMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38","sha":"18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38"}],"sha":"462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/462ccee2267b6414687c17f073ec4de12a6f2c0f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:57:33Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:57:33Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): friction kills + quality of life (Phase E1)\n\n- First-run coach marks: 4 one-time contextual tooltips (options, combo,\n  results, cards toggle); veterans never see them.\n- Friendly error screens with Try again/Home at every load dead-end;\n  developer commands demoted to a collapsed details block.\n- No-repeat sampling for section blitzes (sd_recent ring buffer, last 30).\n- Bank prefetch on tile hover/focus + idle prefetch of the suggested section;\n  loading skeletons replace bare spinners.\n- Review backlog plan: \"18 due - 2 rounds clears it\" + section chips +\n  due-tomorrow whisper; orphan self-heal now toasts instead of silence.\n- QoL: flag-for-review star (sorts first in review), copy-question button,\n  5/10/20 session length (deckLen), streak detail popover.\n- The Ghost: results compare against your previous best run on the section.\n- Dead code sweep: .studyrow removed.\n\nVerified: 47/47 new checks + 30/30 Phase D regression, zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c367fa47fedfc7987d1c00991602d0721142c3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/2c367fa47fedfc7987d1c00991602d0721142c3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDE4YjU4MTQyN2VkOTFiNjlkY2JhMzM2YzMyZGVjYTE3YTRmMWJlMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7","sha":"b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7"}],"sha":"18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/18b581427ed91b69dcba336c32deca17a4f1be38"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:53:36Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:53:36Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(ml): complete Mermaid parity — last 4 case-study architecture diagrams\n\nConverts the ASCII system-architecture/pipeline diagrams in the 4 remaining NLP\ncase studies to appeal-first Mermaid (the files a prior session-limited diagram\nagent never reached). All 27 ml/ case studies now carry Mermaid.\n\n- design_real_time_personalization: 1 block → 2 flowcharts (sync serving + async pipeline)\n- design_semantic_search_engine: 1 flowchart (FAISS+BM25 → RRF → cross-encoder rerank)\n- design_question_answering_system: 3 flowcharts (retriever→reader, multi-hop, eval gate)\n- design_ner_pipeline: 3 flowcharts (BERT-CRF serving + active-learning loop, eval, trace)\n\nAlignment-critical ASCII (nested-NER token→tag grid) and numeric capacity worksheets\ndeliberately kept ASCII per policy. 447/447 ml/ mermaid fences parse-validated (mermaid@11).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cdd74b9b7600f7ddd300700d9cfe5d4470ebedb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/0cdd74b9b7600f7ddd300700d9cfe5d4470ebedb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGIwMDIxYWI4NjgwYjFhY2JjM2Q5NGZlZGQyNWRjMTk5MDFiZjBhZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c","sha":"0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c"}],"sha":"b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/b0021ab8680b1acbc3d94fedd25dc19901bf0af7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:47:16Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:47:16Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(ml): zero-to-hero audit — new modules, NLP deep-dives, full Mermaid parity, 15-Q&A floor\n\nComprehensive senior-interview audit of the ML section. Content gaps closed with\nzero duplication (cross-linked to llm/, database/ where topics already live),\nmassive visual-learning upgrade, and full game/reader/Q&A compatibility.\n\nNew content (13 files):\n- Modules: interpretability_and_explainability (SHAP/LIME/IG/Grad-CAM),\n  privacy_preserving_ml (DP, FedAvg, secure aggregation, PATE, split learning),\n  multi_task_and_multi_objective_learning (MMoE/PLE/PCGrad/uncertainty weighting),\n  anomaly_detection (Isolation Forest, One-Class SVM, LOF, autoencoder, EVT).\n- Sub-files: unsupervised_learning/gaussian_mixtures_and_em,\n  active_learning_and_weak_supervision/semi_supervised_learning,\n  model_evaluation_and_selection/automl_and_nas.\n- NLP deep-dives (6): word_embeddings, sequence_labeling_and_crf,\n  text_classification, topic_modeling, language_modeling, syntactic_parsing.\n\nSection-wide upgrades:\n- Full Mermaid diagram parity pass — 438 fences across ml/, all parse-validated\n  (mermaid@11), appeal-first per owner policy; math/decision mechanics visualized.\n- Q&A floor standardized to 15 everywhere: 76/76 module + sub-files at/above floor,\n  all extractable (first-sentence 15-220 char rule); no module dropped below.\n- Fixed reserved-keyword node id in ab_testing_for_ml (Mermaid `click` collision).\n\nWiring: ml/README.md (40 modules / 36 sub-files / 22 case studies), ml/CLAUDE.md\nmodule + sub-file tables + cross-reference map, root README.md ML row.\n\nRoot CLAUDE.md: new \"Game / Reader / Q&A Compatibility\" authoring contract so all\nfuture files respect extract.py parsing + reader Mermaid render + STUDY_ORDER rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4c3ba67f77bb28eecde1a7c4808ae0984bd8c20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/f4c3ba67f77bb28eecde1a7c4808ae0984bd8c20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBjYWRjOWEzYzkxYzg3OTIzZWMxZjk2N2ZkODU1OTNmZDQ3OGFhNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649","sha":"1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649"}],"sha":"0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0cadc9a3c91c87923ec1f967fd85593fd478aa6c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:01:59Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T13:01:59Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game/reader): sidebars visible by default on a fresh origin\n\n- First visit with no saved prefs: Contents index defaults on for viewports\n  >=1100px and the module tree for >=1400px (saved prefs always win). A blank\n  right gutter on the Pages origin read as broken.\n- Deep links and dive-deeper opens now synthesize a Study-equivalent nav\n  context from the boot-time index (navFromIndex) so the module file tree and\n  Prev/Next are always available, not only when entered through Study.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a89f79b4602d894c5ae63fb6ea4128fb3670c68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/2a89f79b4602d894c5ae63fb6ea4128fb3670c68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDE3MjRiOWVjOTM4MGViOGVkM2ZjMmM3YTAxZjhmZTQ1NjcxNDU2NDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7","sha":"6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7"}],"sha":"1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1724b9ec9380eb8ed3fc2c7a01f8fe4567145649"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:57:59Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:57:59Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"merge main (A2+B+D) into C — final\n\nMerged baae445 (Phase A2 selection/graph + Phase B progression/drama + Phase D\ncoach) into Phase C. Nine app.js conflicts and one style.css conflict, all\nresolved keeping BOTH sides:\n\n- sfx: [C] seal/capture + [B] bossSting/recovered coexist.\n- renderHome: skyline strip between hero and cards, gauntlet card above the\n  [D] coach topic card + quest row; [D] reboard-aware start button + [C]\n  gauntlet/codex entry points.\n- startDeck: [C] keepOrder short-circuits BOTH [A2] interleave and [B]/A1 boss\n  partition (gauntlet/interview recipe order is untouchable) while [A2]\n  prime/flip plumbing stays intact.\n- gradeAnswer: [B] miss-streak/answerLog + [C] interviewer redemption\n  suppression merged in the wrong branch; [C] ledger/interviewer hook now also\n  skips [A2] prime pretests.\n- gradeCard: [B] recall-streak + [C] flashcard ledger tracking.\n- finish: [B] comeback flag + capsule moments + [C] cAfterSave extras all feed\n  the one queueMoments pass (extras lead).\n- saveDeckSnapshot: [C] interview guard + [A2] prime guard.\n- Router comment reconciled ([C] routes live, [D] #/debrief live).\n- style.css: [A2]/[B]/[D] blocks first, [C] block last.\n\nCross-phase fixes surfaced by QA:\n- seededShuffle existed on both sides with different contracts ([D] rng fn vs\n  [C] seed string) — unified into one polymorphic helper, duplicate removed.\n- Three ?qa=1 window.__qa handles ([C]/[B]/[A2]) clobbered each other — all\n  three now Object.assign into one shared object ([C] progress getter became a\n  progress() method).\n- [B] renderBossIntro deferred callback could fire after the deck advanced or\n  ended (programmatic drivers reach buttons under the overlay) — guarded.\n\nQA: qa_phaseC.mjs rerun + 2 cross-phase spot-checks (gauntlet immune to\ninterleave reorder; [D] coach message renders beside the gauntlet card):\n50/50 pass, zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a9f044c8e5ae4f2c0a25d4bc5b725ac3d545bb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/0a9f044c8e5ae4f2c0a25d4bc5b725ac3d545bb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDZlY2FkMWI4NjEyZjkxMjI5Y2MwZTBkMmY0ZTkwMGZhNTFjYTE5Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6","sha":"59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de","sha":"baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de"}],"sha":"6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/6ecad1b8612f91229cc0e0d2f4e900fa51ca19f7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:41:44Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:41:44Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"merge main (B+D) into A2\n\nMerge 0ec8948 (Phase B career ladder/boss staging/double-down/comeback/\ncapsules + Phase D in-app coach) into the A2 branch, keeping BOTH sides''\nfeatures in every conflicted function.\n\nConflicts resolved (7 hunks in app.js + style.css tail):\n- renderHome listeners: D''s !reboard gate on the review CTA + A2''s\n  confusion-drill/fading listeners (card order: resume, review, coach/\n  reboarding suggested, A2 confusion, A2 fading, weak, rusty)\n- startDeck: B''s resetPhaseBState() + A2''s flip-set/interleave item build;\n  interleave still touches only the non-boss prefix of B''s\n  personalDifficulty partition\n- resumeDeck: state.prime=false + B''s resetPhaseBState()\n- renderQuestion: A2 flip prompt coexists with B''s #comboSlot (dropped the\n  removed inline comboChip from the flip prompt), dd-bar renders after the\n  prompt, skippable guard + B''s ddYes/ddNo listeners\n- gradeAnswer order: A2 confusion tag -> B capsule check -> grading branch\n  (prime/retry/test/normal with B comeback + combo-slot refresh) -> B\n  double-down payout -> buildReveal (B recovered/dd chips + A1 provenance +\n  A2 explain-back)\n- finish: B comeback computation + A2 confusion field on result rows;\n  saveSessionLocal keeps quiet/confusion + B''s comeback history flag\n- style.css: all three tails kept ([A2], B section 19, [D] Coach) — no\n  selector overlap\n\nD''s todayISO()/nowHM() qa_date/qa_time seams: A2''s date-seeded flip gate and\nprime save already route through todayISO(), so the seams cover them.\n\nQA: 45/45 across 3 runs, no console errors — full prior A2 suite updated for\nB moment overlays (click-through on flawless finish) + new spot-checks:\ncombo chip renders in .qhead #comboSlot during a streak (B) and\nstate.today.message renders on Home (D).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe6566e8c419093571481e5682b40d743180c3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/fe6566e8c419093571481e5682b40d743180c3d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGJhYWU0NDU3YzQ3ZDY4ZTIxNWMyNTY5ZjAyNmQ1MzU1N2I4OWM3ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931","sha":"277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692","sha":"0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692"}],"sha":"baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/baae4457c47d68e215c2569f026d53557b89c7de"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:36:09Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:36:09Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"merge main into C; adapt to Phase 0/A1 architecture\n\nMerged bbbf3a0 (Phase 0 Pages-only pivot + Phase A1 answer-flow core) and\nswapped every Phase-C stand-in for the real infrastructure:\n\n- c_cyrb53/c_mulberry32/c_seededShuffle -> main''s cyrb53/mulberry32; kept a\n  seededShuffle helper (main lacked one) beside the PRNG helpers.\n- c_moment/c_queueMoments/c_tone/c_MOMENT_SFX -> main''s moments engine.\n  cAfterSave() now returns moment entries fed into queueMoments'' new `extra`\n  slot (deck headlines lead); codex capture/foil diffs ride progressSnapshot''s\n  new [C] codex field — one snapshot pass, one overlay system. New sfx\n  one-liners: seal(), capture().\n- c_dispatch/c_go + the isolated hashchange listener -> DELETED; #/gauntlet,\n  #/codex, #/interview/<sec> wired into main''s dispatch() reserved slots,\n  navigation via main''s go()/redirect().\n- answer()-era hooks -> gradeAnswer''s grade path (post-confidence): ledger\n  tracking (long_memory / restored / comeback) on first attempts only,\n  interviewer HP/crit/follow-up after buildReveal. The wrong-answer follow-up\n  swaps the next still-pending deck slot in place (no orphaned items at\n  finish); the A1 redemption requeue is suppressed inside an interview.\n  deepReads counts dive-deeper opens from miss reveals in buildReveal.\n- Gauntlet runs through startDeck''s new keepOrder opt (no shuffle/boss,\n  forced MCQ mode, confidence step stays); sd_active_deck snapshot/resume\n  restores the frozen qids order + gauntlet flags and replay; interview decks\n  skip the snapshot (leaving reschedules).\n- Heatmap gold dots re-anchored; ledger strip on Progress; loadProgress\n  backfills awards/deepReads (localStorage-only).\n- CSS folded into main''s .moment overlay (seal-stamp + card-flip icon add-ons\n  only); gauntlet/codex/skyline/ledger/interview classes kept; daylight-theme\n  contrast overrides added for the gold accents.\n- vt(): swallow the benign AbortError the ViewTransition ready/finished\n  promises raise when rapid navigation skips a transition.\n\nQA (qa_phaseC.mjs, rewritten for two-step answering): 48/48 pass, zero\nconsole errors (no /api calls remain).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6209b16d19c4e1c40f59d8d4776f5d9d7b6ac5e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/6209b16d19c4e1c40f59d8d4776f5d9d7b6ac5e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDU5YWU5YTJiY2JhMTRlYzY0NjZiOGM5ZWYwMGVmZGY5NDU4M2Q1ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604","sha":"71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","sha":"bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079"}],"sha":"59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/59ae9a2bcba14ec6466b8c9ef00efdf94583d5e6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:26:03Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:26:03Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"merge main into A2; adapt to Phase 0/A1 architecture\n\nMerge bbbf3a0 (Phase 0 Pages-only pivot + Phase A1 answer-flow core) into the\nA2 branch. app.js/style.css conflicts resolved by taking main''s files as the\nbase and re-applying every A2 feature adapted to the new architecture.\n\nDedup deletions (superseded by main):\n- self-shipped a2Hash/a2Rand -> main''s cyrb53/mulberry32\n- client-side distractorIds/concepts derivation (provIndexFor/conceptsOf) ->\n  bank fields directly (regenerated banks carry distractorIds/concepts/\n  sourceFile/*Md); flip options resolve via bankById + q.distractorIds\n- text-match distractorSource -> main''s src-index distractorSource\n- own .prov style + .sheet-overlay/.sheet -> main''s .prov and the\n  .pause-sheet/.pause-card pattern (#primeSheet id)\n\nAdaptations:\n- Confusion recording moved into gradeAnswer''s wrong path (same src resolution\n  as A1 provenance); result rows carry `confusion`; tally + cap-50 in\n  saveSessionLocal; skipped for flip items\n- Explain-back mounts in buildReveal (first-attempt wrong AND failed\n  redemption) and revealCard; matches against bank `concepts`; ported\n  tokenizer used for the USER text only; E toggle + textarea shortcut guard\n- Prime bypasses the A1 confidence bar (answer() -> gradeAnswer(i, null)),\n  never snapshots (saveDeckSnapshot guard), never raises the pause sheet\n  (guardedNav/onHashChange treat prime as leave-silently), forces quiz mode,\n  saves via saveSessionLocal {quiet:true} (review records only), restores the\n  study hash before opening the reader\n- Flip rounds: flipOptsFor(q) keeps main''s src/optOrder semantics so snapshot\n  resume rebuilds flips (flip flag persisted); works under hard-deck gating\n  and the confidence step; provenance + explain-back skipped on flips;\n  mulberry32(cyrb53(date+qid)) < 0.3 gate unchanged\n- startDeck opts {hard, prime, flip, interleave}: interleave applies to the\n  NON-BOSS prefix only (personalDifficulty boss partition untouched); hard and\n  flash decks interleave after their shuffle\n- Memory map / fading card / confusion drill card merged into main''s\n  renderHome (after resume/review cards) and openStudySection node rendering\n\nQA (rewritten for two-step answering; prime asserted to skip the confidence\nbar): 43/43 across 3 runs, no console errors, incl. full-blitz regression\nthrough miss-loop redemptions and skip-teach cards.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4d3761e3ebab6861e4d4591ad0fe4a17e47e50f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/4d3761e3ebab6861e4d4591ad0fe4a17e47e50f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDI3N2JkMzM4MWY0MTEwYmRmNDU2NWZkM2Q4YzRkMzMzMThiOGY5MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069","sha":"c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","sha":"bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079"}],"sha":"277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/277bd3381f4110bdf4565fd3d8c4d33318b8f931"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:19:46Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:19:46Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"Merge branch ''worktree-agent-a4e01d5ff4b5acce5''\n\n# Conflicts:\n#\tsrc/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/style.css","tree":{"sha":"e13cfbe525b4ab7ae99a6933b94141243672be5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/e13cfbe525b4ab7ae99a6933b94141243672be5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBlYzg5NDhjNTk5ZDY2ZGU2NDRhMTdiODMxNzU5NTY4MGY4OWQ2OTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174","sha":"dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7","sha":"15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7"}],"sha":"0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0ec8948c599d66de644a17b8317595680f89d692"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:18:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:18:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Phase D — in-app coach (daily pick, reboarding, Friday Debrief, quests, streak nudge)\n\nAdds the terse, specific coach voice on top of the existing hash router and\nmoments engine: coachPick() ports the old pick_today.py selection logic\n(unplayed -> weakest -> least-seen, never repeating yesterday unless forced),\na ~32-template message bank picks true specifics (accuracy deltas, due\ncounts, streak proximity) via a seeded, memory-aware selector, and the\nreboarding protocol replaces the suggested card (never guilts) after a >2-day\ngap. Adds the Friday Debrief (#/debrief: week strip, per-section deltas,\nmoment-of-the-week, three live-progress quests) and a same-day 4pm streak\nnudge. All new state lives in sd_coach, additive to sd_progress. All coach\ncode is a single delimited region with small marked insertions into\nboot()/dispatch()/renderHome() to keep the merge surface small alongside the\nother in-flight phases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7f4fd1e500b252b9a20117362184a9bc1bddf4d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/7f4fd1e500b252b9a20117362184a9bc1bddf4d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDE1YTE0ZDhlMmE2NTAyNzRkZWJhN2RhYWM0ZWFmMDgzOGMyNjMxZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","sha":"bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079"}],"sha":"15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/15a14d8e2a650274deba7daac4eaf0838c2631f7"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:14:30Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:14:30Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Phase B — career ladder, boss staging, double-down, comeback, capsules\n\nProgression, drama, and celebration on top of the Phase A1 answer-flow core:\n\n- Career ladder: LEVEL_TITLES bands (Intern -> Fellow), a 22px progress ring\n  around the topbar Lv chip, and a bigger title-promotion moment (confetti)\n  layered onto the existing level-up moment.\n- Results reward moments: daily goal ring + \"N to go\" line, an elapsed\n  stopwatch badge (+ \"under 5 minutes\" chip), and a streak-advance line, all\n  on the results screen.\n- Boss staging: a 1.2s tap/key-to-skip interstitial the first time the deck\n  reaches a boss item, body.boss-mode dims the backdrop toward warn/gold, and\n  a \"Boss cleared: n/m\" badge on results.\n- Double-down: a one-time offer bar before the last question of a quiz deck\n  (>=70% accuracy, >=3 answered) that doubles or loses the session''s bonus XP\n  so far, with an outcome note on the reveal and a D keyboard shortcut.\n- Comeback engine: a correct answer after >=2 consecutive misses earns a\n  \"Recovered.\" chip + 5 bonus XP; a session with a >=3 miss streak that ends\n  on 5 straight corrects gets a \"Comeback\" badge (history.comeback).\n- Combo HUD: moved from an inline .qtext chip (which reflowed the question)\n  into a reserved-width slot in .qhead, updated live from gradeAnswer.\n- Flashcard juice: a recall-streak chip, sfx.combo() at 3/5/7-in-a-row, and a\n  3D card-flip reveal (REDUCED-gated).\n- Time capsules: a flawless (10/10, no redemptions) quiz blitz buries its\n  hardest question 60 days out (rv.capsule); answering a due capsule\n  correctly fires a \"it kept\" moment (max one new capsule per day).\n\nThis worktree had forked before Phase 0 (Pages-only pivot) and Phase A1\n(answer-flow core, moments engine) landed on main, so main was merged in\nfirst to build on the real infrastructure rather than stubbing it out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b1ba781c428539c75d37b1255b02edfcfb1cb3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/0b1ba781c428539c75d37b1255b02edfcfb1cb3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGRlZTk2NGEyZWZiMDRmMGM0MWE1NDE5MWEwNGE1MGRlNDM5NTUxNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","sha":"bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079"}],"sha":"dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/dee964a2efb04f0c41a54191a04a50de43955174"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:12:03Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:12:03Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Phase C tentpoles — Gauntlet, Codex, Skyline, Ledger, Interviewer\n\nAdds the five Phase-C features to the daily learning game, built against this\nworktree''s pre-Phase-0 base (the brief''s \"already built\" moment engine, PRNG and\nhash router are absent here). Missing infra is provided as MINIMAL local\nstand-ins prefixed c_ inside one delimited [C] block, with single call sites, so\na later `git merge main` cannot collide with the real identically-named helpers\nand the swap is cheap. All shared-function edits (renderHome/finish/answer/\nrenderQuestion/renderProgress/openStudySection/heatmapHTML/startDeck/boot) are\nsmall marked /* [C] */ blocks.\n\n- The Gauntlet: daily sealed 10-question run, deterministic recipe (oldest due →\n  suggested → weakest → final advanced), frozen in localStorage sd_gauntlet;\n  finishing seals (+40 bonus XP, wax-seal moment), one scored attempt/day, replay\n  routes to unscored practice; gold heatmap dots on gauntlet days.\n- The Codex: codexState() derives held/needed/captured/foil/tarnished purely from\n  review records; shelf screen at #/codex; capture/foil moments diffed in finish().\n- The Skyline: ambient inline-SVG retention city on Home, one building per\n  captured module grouped into section districts; hidden when 0 captured.\n- The Ledger: progress.awards (only new persisted object) + progress.deepReads;\n  9 client-detected achievements with earned/hint chips on Progress and moments.\n- The Interviewer: Silver-gated boss battle (#/interview/<sec>), typewriter intro,\n  12-HP bar with combo crits, and graph-driven follow-ups drawn from the most\n  related module on a wrong answer; win writes interview_/panel_ awards.\n\nNew persisted fields: progress.awards, progress.deepReads, localStorage\nsd_gauntlet. Headless CDP QA (qa_phaseC.mjs): 37/37 pass, no real JS errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da709c8803b5b075be4e467585390cab052caddf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/da709c8803b5b075be4e467585390cab052caddf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDcxZjgxMjMzNDY4NTFkOWVmYmU4Y2E2ODkyY2YwZTVlYTViMjk2MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","sha":"a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94"}],"sha":"71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/71f8123346851d9efbe8ca6892cf0e5ea5b29604"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:04:14Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T12:04:14Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Phase A2 selection/graph learning features\n\nAdds five graph- and selection-aware learning features to the daily game,\nbuilt on the current single-step answering base (this worktree predates the\nPhase A1 confidence flow; all hooks land in the real answer()/renderQuestion/\nstartReview paths). distractorIds and concepts are derived client-side since\nthe committed bank schema does not carry them yet.\n\n1. Confusion-aware interleaving\n   - loadGraph() (graphCache, 404-tolerant); orderInterleaved() greedy reorder\n     (no consecutive same-module, highest-remaining-count first, graph-connected\n     tiebreak). Applied to the NON-BOSS prefix in startBlitz (graph pairs) and\n     startReview/drill/refresh (module-only) via a new startDeck opts.interleave.\n   - Confusion tracking: wrong cross-module picks resolve provenance\n     (distractorSource text-match) and record progress.confusions[\"<a>|<b>\"]\n     (canonical, cap 50). Amber home card drills the top mixed-up pair.\n\n2. Module Memory Map\n   - moduleStats() retention/held/overdue aggregation. Learning-path nodes tint\n     mm-fresh/warm/fading/cold + mm-overdue pulse, retention in tooltip/aria.\n   - \"Fading this week\" home card -> exact refresh deck (state.section=refresh).\n\n3. Prime (pretest before reading)\n   - Interstitial for never-quizzed modules (>=3 Qs); 3 core-difficulty guesses,\n     no XP/combo/snapshot (state.prime, quiet saveSessionLocal writing only\n     review records as \"learned\"), then opens the reader. sd_prime_opt opt-out.\n\n4. Explain-Back\n   - Optional \"say it in your own words (E)\" on wrong reveals + flashcard reveals.\n     Ported tokenizer + derived concepts -> \"key terms covered k/N\", .hit/.missterm\n     glows, +5 XP once/question for >=8 words.\n\n5. Flip rounds\n   - ~30% of review items (deterministic per day+qid) whose 3 distractors all\n     resolve become answer->question flips; provenance skipped for flips.\n\nNew persisted fields: progress.confusions, localStorage sd_prime_opt.\nNew CSS: .prov, .explain-back/.eb-*, .hit, .missterm, .flip-eyebrow/.flip-item,\n.review-card.confuse/.fading, .sheet-overlay/.sheet, .pathnode.mm-*.\nQA (headless CDP, /tmp/qa_phaseA2.mjs): 32/32 across 3 runs, no JS errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"654f479aec3aead3cc82f19694a4401a65300284","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/654f479aec3aead3cc82f19694a4401a65300284"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGM1YjVmNjk0ZWM4MTRhYmU1YjJmMWQwNjQ2M2NlZjg4NmJjZTAwNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","sha":"a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94"}],"sha":"c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/c5b5f694ec814abe5b2f1d06463cef886bce0069"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T11:32:42Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T11:32:42Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): answer-flow learning core (Phase A1)\n\n- Miss Loop: wrong answers re-enter the deck ~3 questions later as a\n  Redemption round (+5 flat XP on redeem; first attempt stays honest for\n  SM-2); results split Redeemed vs Still shaky.\n- Honest why-wrong: picking a distractor shows the real question it answers\n  (distractorIds provenance) with a read-that-instead link; dive-deeper now\n  opens the exact source file; miss review expands to the full answer.\n- Recall-first review: review/weak decks hide options behind \"Show options\n  (Space)\" for a genuine retrieval attempt; 1.5x XP on hard decks.\n- Confidence calibration: Sure/Not-sure step before feedback; wrong+sure\n  eases harder (-0.3) with hypercorrection styling; correct+unsure grows\n  interval slower; per-section calibration tallies; flashcards upgraded to\n  Missed/Hard/Easy.\n- Skip-to-teach 2.0: skip shows a concept card with cloze-blurred key terms,\n  then re-tests 3+ questions later with no answer visible; wrong lock-ins now\n  record honestly as wrong.\n- Calibrated difficulty: personal difficulty from lapses/ease/latency drives\n  boss selection and a \"hard for you\" chip; slow corrects schedule shorter.\n- qInline(): inline code/bold rendering in questions, options, reveals.\n\nVerified: 31/31 headless CDP checks (qa_phaseA), zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8085fc122911e7f354625d5d9878e70cb5467d3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/8085fc122911e7f354625d5d9878e70cb5467d3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGJiYmYzYTBlYzM3NzY2NDVhZTE4YTFkNDQ4YjU2NmEyMWJlNjAwNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409","sha":"40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409"}],"sha":"bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/bbbf3a0ec3776645ae18a1d448b566a21be60079"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T11:02:13Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T11:02:13Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Pages-only pivot — foundation for the full-vision build (Phase 0)\n\n- Drop the entire local stack (server.py, state/, scheduling/, pick_today.py,\n  claude_coach_prompt.md): localStorage sd_progress is now the single source\n  of truth; app.js loses IS_STATIC/apiGet/apiPost/pending-session replay.\n- extract.py: emit distractorIds (provenance), sourceFile, concepts (top-6 IDF\n  tokens), and *Md display variants (only when they differ); drop qIndex from\n  output. All 5,772 baseline question ids verified byte-identical.\n- Hash router (#/home, #/quiz/<sec>, #/reader/<path>…): browser Back now closes\n  the reader / pauses a quiz instead of exiting the site; deep links work.\n- Session guard: sd_active_deck snapshots after every answer; pause sheet\n  (Keep playing / Pause & leave / Finish now with partial credit); same-day\n  resume card on Home restores the deck pixel-identically.\n- Moments engine: queued full-screen celebrations diffed from pre/post progress\n  (level-up, streak milestones, tier promotion, first gold, backlog zero,\n  daily goal) with new oscillator tones; REDUCED-motion aware.\n- Telemetry: per-answer response time (EMA on review records), session duration.\n- Durability: export/import progress JSON + backup nudge; PWA (manifest +\n  service worker, cache-first shell, stale-while-revalidate banks) with\n  __BUILD__ stamping in pages.yml; pages.yml also rebuilds graph/*.json.\n- Fix: normalize empty hash to #/home at boot; add SVG favicon.\n\nVerified: 15/15 headless CDP smoke checks, zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"80b58696f7abe578df09bc6685565cf1094bff79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/80b58696f7abe578df09bc6685565cf1094bff79"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDQwZmE5YTllMTAyOWJjYWYyNGEyZWQ5ZTc4ZDZlNTk1YzFlMzc0MDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","sha":"a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94"}],"sha":"40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/40fa9a9e1029bcaf24a2ed9e78d6e595c1e37409"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T18:32:15Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T18:32:15Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game/reader): per-type Mermaid chart rendering — color, font scale, overflow\n\nScreenshot audit of every mermaid type in the repo (273 fences: 211 flowchart,\n25 xychart-beta, 15 sequence, 9 stateDiagram-v2, 5 quadrantChart, 4 pie,\n4 timeline — all in llm/) found the chart family rendering with default dark-\ntheme colors (near-invisible) and text scaled far below prose size. All fixes\nare reader-global in app.js; zero source-file workarounds.\n\nPer-type fixes:\n- pie: One Dark pie1-12 slice palette (an 80% slice was literally invisible\n  black-on-black before), gold title, dark % labels; when legend+title force a\n  downscale, re-render with text boosted toward ~13px displayed (measure ->\n  boost -> refine, title tracks the boost at 16/14); legend rows re-spaced and\n  swatches resized to the boosted font.\n- xychart-beta: transparent plot background (was an opaque black slab), gold\n  title, One Dark plotColorPalette, #abb2bf axis text; injected per-render\n  init directive sizes the chart to the column width so labels keep true size;\n  long titles font-fitted to the chart width (was overflowing + clipping the\n  last tick label); colliding x tick labels rotate -28 with anchor end.\n- quadrantChart: One Dark tinted quadrant fills + hue-matched quadrant labels,\n  blue points; chart rendered at column width via injected directive;\n  colliding point labels flip above their point (quadrant-name labels seeded\n  as obstacles; three candidate positions tried).\n- timeline: cScale0-11 replaced with saturated One Dark cycle + dark labels\n  (2017/2018 period boxes were near-black), title gold (font-size attr is\n  \"4ex\" — computed px check), horizontal axis line was mainBkg #1a1a1a ->\n  #4b5263; wide timelines keep a 0.75x text-scale floor and h-scroll like a\n  film strip instead of shrinking to 0.20x (microscopic) as before.\n\nQA evidence (headless Chrome, CDP, saveSession stubbed): 18 diagram cases\nscreenshotted per round across 5 rounds in default pane + fullscreen +\nlightbox + daylight/nebula themes; regression guard re-shot mcp_client_\npatterns (sequence), durable_long_running_agents (state), lora (flowchart) —\nunchanged; no console errors; node --check passes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"828237dcbeba56705d3af0e64aa6fe3268b58275","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/828237dcbeba56705d3af0e64aa6fe3268b58275"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGE1NzA0NWE1ODEyZmI2OTY1NzA3Nzg3ODcyZWNhODllNDA2ZjliOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d","sha":"906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d"}],"sha":"a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a57045a5812fb6965707787872eca89e406f9b94"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:42:52Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:42:52Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(game): consistent diagram coloring + sequence font sizing in the reader\n\nSequence and state diagrams can''t use the flowchart classDef palette, so\nthey rendered flat gray next to fully-colored flowcharts (user report).\nSequence diagrams are now themed from the same One Dark palette via\nthemeVariables (blue actors, gold notes/signal text, purple loop frames)\nwith wrap enabled and 13-14px fonts — fixes both the oversized text and\nnotes overflowing their boxes. State diagrams (and any future palette-less\nflowchart) get a per-node One Dark tint fallback: only nodes still wearing\nthe default mainBkg gray are tinted, authored colors are never touched.\n\nAlso: viewBox expansion pass for mermaid''s under-measured long-mono-line\nlayouts, and an explicit affordance for horizontally scrollable diagrams\n(pinned edge glow that fades at the scroll ends + persistent\n\"scroll · zoom\" hint) so overflow reads as scrollable, not clipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"844556b0761e96f876d594f78edbc23591b101ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/844556b0761e96f876d594f78edbc23591b101ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDkwNjM5MGZmMDVkNzYzOWNiZWU0YjdmY2FhZjRjMzJkNzgxNTNiMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf","sha":"9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf"}],"sha":"906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/906390ff05d7639cbee4b7fcaaf4c32d78153b0d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:25:47Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:25:47Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): soften all four themes; retry Pages deploys through queue backups\n\nThemes: desaturate the aurora-mesh blobs and lower their opacity in every\ntheme (midnight 0.30->0.25, orchid 0.26->0.22, ember 0.24->0.20, daylight\n0.55->0.46); ember''s second accent calms from #ef4444 to #f87171; swatches\nmatch the new mesh colors. Verified via headless screenshots on all four.\n\nCI: deploy-pages clamps its timeout input to a 10-min max (the 1800000 in\nab4e9e7 was silently capped), so chain up to 3 deploy attempts instead —\neach failed attempt cancels its own deployment cleanly before the next.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4de32f3183bf740dd5706e9e729f2ef8f8193602","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/4de32f3183bf740dd5706e9e729f2ef8f8193602"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDlmN2VhNDA3NDg1MTg0OGFjMjMzMzRjMjkyMDk4ZTBkZmEyNTQ1Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039","sha":"ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039"}],"sha":"9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9f7ea4074851848ac23334c292098e0dfa2545cf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:12:02Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T17:12:02Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(ci): wait up to 30 min for queued Pages deployments\n\nThe Pages deploy queue backed up past deploy-pages'' default 600s timeout;\nthe action then failed the job while the deployment was still queued and\ncancelled it during cleanup. Raise the action timeout to 30 min (job cap\n40 min) so a slow queue is a delay, not a failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87b1d8b7ee2247ce0174173d8b4cca1243f6b6ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/87b1d8b7ee2247ce0174173d8b4cca1243f6b6ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGFiNGU5ZTdjMWQzNzg0ZWU3MjNmNWM5NjY3OTgyNmY2OGM5YWQwMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b","sha":"1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b"}],"sha":"ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/ab4e9e7c1d3784ee723f5c96679826f68c9ad039"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:57:56Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:57:56Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(ci): don''t cancel in-progress Pages deploys — cancellation races kill the next deployment\n\nTwo rapid pushes (e51843e then 6a3c784) reproduced the known deploy-pages\nrace: cancel-in-progress killed the first run mid-deploy, and its cleanup\ncancelled the site''s latest Pages deployment — which by then was the new\nrun''s, so 6a3c784''s deploy failed with \"Deployment cancelled.\" Queue runs\ninstead, matching GitHub''s official Pages starter workflow.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a1ae681ee5194c108439f9c4d6a803f21145324e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/a1ae681ee5194c108439f9c4d6a803f21145324e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDFhYWY2MjM2NGYxNjQyYmY1NmFmZTdmNWY3ZGNiMjI5MWM3MWQ1MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068","sha":"6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068"}],"sha":"1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1aaf62364f1642bf56afe7f5f7dcb2291c71d51b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:45:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:45:04Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm): wave-2 content sweep — 181 Q&As, 293 understanding aids, 63 chart upgrades across 145 files\n\n14 sweep agents covered all 166 llm files with three jobs: top up every\nbelow-floor file to the 15-Q&A minimum (gotchas-first ordering), add\nmissing understanding aids (intuition hooks, concrete numbers, broken->fix\npairs, cross-links — llm linked module pairs grew 50 -> 151), and upgrade\nremaining ASCII bars/curves/timelines/state-machines to appeal-first\nMermaid (xychart-beta, pie, quadrantChart, timeline, stateDiagram-v2).\n\n3 adversarial reviewers + fixer pass: both must-fix findings repaired\n(DeepSeek $5.5M cost re-attributed to V3; fabricated cl100k-vs-GPT-2\ndigit-tokenization contrast replaced with tiktoken-verified facts), plus\nfollow-up fixes for every substantive nice-to-have: duplicate RadixAttention\nand byte-level-BPE Q&As deduped, self-hosting case study reconciled\n($36K bill, GPT-4-class-was-overkill narrative), Anthropic multi-agent stat\ncorrected to the published 90.2%-over-baseline result, both lost-in-the-middle\ncharts aligned to Liu et al. 2023''s real figures (92/70/54/69/90), LR-schedule\nchart resampled to an even 10% grid, quadrantChart cost anchors restored.\n\nValidation: all 273 mermaid fences parse under real mermaid v11 (headless\nChrome, was 210 pre-wave); all 125 files with interview sections now >= 15\nQ&As (was 44 below); ASCII lint errors down 62 -> 28; extract.py rebuilt the\nbank (llm 1362 -> 1543 questions; content-stable ids preserve review state);\nbuild_graph.py regenerated all 12 section graphs (llm edges 158 -> 180).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1dedf73efd3d11bd442fd2269aa9651088f499b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/c1dedf73efd3d11bd442fd2269aa9651088f499b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDZhM2M3ODRhOGExMjU2YWM0ODM4YzMyYjc5YjZjNDZjZTEwMDEwNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b","sha":"95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b"}],"sha":"6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/6a3c784a8a1256ac4838c32b79b6c46ce1001068"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:34:59Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:34:59Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): landscape Learning Path — multi-column serpentine, gutter-routed edges, live filter\n\nLayout: the path screen escapes main''s 780px column (.path-screen breakout,\ncapped at 1560px) and lays chips out as a width-adaptive boustrophedon grid —\n1 column on mobile, 2 at ~900px, up to 4 on landscape laptops (~330px/col),\nsnaking row 1 left->right, row 2 right->left. Chips compacted (9px padding,\n13.5px titles) with ~62px row gutters: the 52-topic LLM section drops from\n>10,000px to ~2,000px total page height (~2 screenfuls at 1512x982).\n\nEdge routing: prerequisite chords are routed orthogonally (rounded subway\ncorners via a new orthPath() helper) through the chip-free row gutters and\ncolumn gaps only; greedy interval-coloring assigns parallel lanes per\ngutter/gap and chord mouths spread across each chip edge, so no chord ever\ncrosses chip text. Local hops (within one gutter) draw by default; multi-row\nstaircases (.wk) and lexical-only pairs stay hidden until a chip is hovered\nor keyboard-focused, which spotlights all its edges and dims the rest.\nLayout + routing recompute on fan toggle, filter, and debounced resize.\n\nFilter fix: typing now hides non-matching chips and re-flows the grid so\nmatches gather compactly at the top, shows an \"N of M topics\" count\n(aria-live announced), Enter opens the first match''s reader, and clearing\n(including the native x / Esc) restores the full path. Chords with a hidden\nendpoint are suppressed while filtering.\n\nPreserved: leaf-fan expansion (rows below shift, no overlap), practiced\ncheckmark, \"you are here\" ring, click-to-reader with Previous/Next context,\nkeyboard focusability, entrance stagger + reduced-motion behavior, and\ntoken-driven colors across all 4 themes.\n\nQA (headless-Chrome CDP, screenshots reviewed): LLM at 1512x982 and\n1728x1117 -> 4 columns, pageH ~2,000px, 0 chord-over-chip-text hits in\n22,500 sampled path points, no horizontal scrollbar; focus on chip 24 lit\n10 chords / 11 linked chips with the rest dimmed; filter \"guardrails\" ->\n\"1 of 52 topics\" gathered at top and Enter opened the Guardrails reader,\nclear restored 52; filter \"agent\" -> 7 matches re-flowed into 2 rows;\nBook (13) and LLD (7) render clean partial rows; daylight + ember themes\nverified; 19-file fan opened with 0 step overlaps; 900x900 collapses to\n2 columns cleanly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1605c8a6fb01b3c7205eb3728cc1925e446862d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/1605c8a6fb01b3c7205eb3728cc1925e446862d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDk1YWQ3ZmYwNzM1ZDBiZGQ1Nzc5YjVmZTRlM2EzNzRhMmQxMzIwM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301","sha":"e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301"}],"sha":"95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/95ad7ff0735d0bdd5779b5fe4e3a374a2d13203b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:08:46Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T16:08:46Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): widescreen diagrams + theme refresh\n\nReader mermaid rendering is now landscape-aware: every directional diagram\n(flowchart/graph TD-LR, stateDiagram direction) is rendered in both\norientations off-screen and the reader keeps the one that reads better at\nthe current column width — flipped text never drops below 0.7x, spills into\nthe prose-column side gutters in fullscreen (max-width 860px stays for\nprose), and h-scrolls past that. The choice re-evaluates live via a\ndebounced ResizeObserver when the reader is dragged wider / fullscreened.\nEvery diagram gets a corner drag-grip (freeform resize, no upper cap,\ndouble-click resets); source files stay untouched so GitHub keeps the\nauthored orientation.\n\nThemes: midnight drops its teal mesh blob (pure blue/violet now), aurora is\nretired (saved prefs fall back to midnight at pre-paint), new Orchid\n(purple/pink) theme, Ember reworked to a true red/orange spectrum.\n\nQA: headless-Chrome CDP pass — 4 themes + retired-pref fallback + popover,\norientation flip pane->fullscreen->pane (1321px tall TD becomes 208px LR),\ngrip drag/reset, zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34d70ceee943a45d0c3a6a9227b503cb790d93c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/34d70ceee943a45d0c3a6a9227b503cb790d93c3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGU1MTg0M2U0YTUzNWE0NjUwNjg4N2MyZjBlNTgyZGUzMjRmMTAzMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25","sha":"63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25"}],"sha":"e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/e51843e4a535a46506887c2f0e582de324f10301"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T15:31:07Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T15:31:07Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): appeal-first conversion wave — 60 new diagrams, all 210 fences parse-validated\n\n13-agent sweep over 122 llm files under the new appeal-first policy:\nevery untagged ASCII fence classified against the /mermaid-diagrams\nchecklist; 60 true directed flowcharts converted to Mermaid (verbatim\nOne-Dark 7-class palette, semantic class per node, captions preserved\nor added from surrounding numbers); ~500 blocks deliberately kept ASCII\n(grids/masks, memory maps, before/after stat pairs, bar charts, linear\nchains that read fine — per-file rationale recorded in the run report).\n\nAlso repaired existing fences across 12 files: classDef blocks that sat\nAFTER node definitions (silent class failures), non-canonical partial\npalettes replaced with the standard 7-class block, and redundant\nper-diagram init directives dropped. Fixed 3 pre-existing broken\ndiagrams the sweep surfaced: unquoted labels containing parens/quotes\n(framework_observability, speculative_decoding) and semicolons inside\nsequenceDiagram messages/notes acting as statement separators\n(agent_durability_patterns).\n\nVerification: every one of the 210 mermaid fences in llm/ now parses\nclean under real mermaid v11 (the same CDN build GitHub and the game\nreader use), via a headless-Chrome mermaid.parse() harness. ASCII lint\nerrors are down 64 -> 62 vs HEAD (none introduced).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"04929544c15624b856374558beb3db2bb8d223a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/04929544c15624b856374558beb3db2bb8d223a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDYzZDBmM2Q1NTY4MWM4NzhkOTdkMTkwMDUxNTRjYTdiOThiYjJlMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72","sha":"2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72"}],"sha":"63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/63d0f3d55681c878d97d19005154ca7b98bb2e25"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:51:12Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:51:12Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): weighted prerequisite edges on the Learning Path\n\nOverlay the Study screen''s serpentine Learning Path with weighted\nprerequisite chords from graph/<section>.json (built by build_graph.py\nfrom real repo cross-links + lexical Q&A overlap — nothing invented).\n\n- Data: undirected pairs are oriented forward along the existing path\n  order at render time (earlier module -> later module); pairs whose\n  modules aren''t on the rendered path are dropped, and consecutive\n  pairs are skipped since the spine already implies them. A missing or\n  failed graph fetch renders the v1 path unchanged.\n- Rendering: one SVG bezier per pair in a group under the spine; weight\n  maps to a 1-5px stroke via a --sw custom prop. Link-backed pairs are\n  solid accent at 0.5 opacity; lexical-only pairs stay hidden until\n  hover. Same-column pairs bracket out through a reserved outer lane\n  (so arcs never pass under chip text); cross-column pairs take a\n  gentle arc through the chip-free middle gap with mid-x jitter clamped\n  to the gap width. Chord geometry recomputes on the existing\n  layoutPath/resize path.\n- Highlight: pointerenter/leave on chips + delegated focusin/focusout\n  spotlight a node''s chords (full opacity, 1.3x thicker, lexical edges\n  faint dashed) and dim unconnected chords and chips to ~0.3 — pure\n  class toggles, no per-frame JS, instant under reduced motion.\n- Legend under the hero (mono/muted) reports N cross-links mapped;\n  zero-link sections (database, book, lld) say \"no cross-link data yet\n  — path order shown\" and draw no default chords. Chip aria-labels\n  gain \", connects to K other topics\".\n- QA: node --check + CDP script (qa-edges.mjs, port 9233) against the\n  live server — llm renders 40 solid chords (<= 50 link-backed pairs),\n  keyboard focus on inference_and_decoding highlights 10 chords + 3\n  dashed lexical and dims others to 0.3, blur restores, database shows\n  zero chords, daylight theme legible, zero console exceptions;\n  screenshots reviewed for hairballs/chip-text crossings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"032dbe85318f7637627f6c56c130da2eafee2813","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/032dbe85318f7637627f6c56c130da2eafee2813"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDJmZWY4MDE1MTJmOWUyNmFmODg2Njg1NTZkY2VlOTQ0MTBlMDZhNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934","sha":"63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934"}],"sha":"2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2fef801512f9e26af88668556dcee94410e06a72"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:37:54Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:37:54Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): Learning Path graph replaces Study topic list\n\nThe flat .studyrow list in openStudySection is now a serpentine\nskill-tree: glass node chips (mono step number, module name, Q count)\nabsolutely positioned over an SVG spine of gradient cubic beziers\n(--accent to --accent-2), two columns on >=700px and one centered\ncolumn below, laid out in JS with a debounced resize handler; vertical\nscroll is the navigation.\n\nData sources (zero fabrication): the path order is modulesOf(bank),\ni.e. STUDY_ORDER with unlisted modules appended; expandable leaf fans\ncome from index.json''s files map (multi-file modules only, labels\nmatching buildModuleNav); the practiced check-mark derives from\nstate.progress.reviews module keys; the pulsing \"you are here\" ring\nfrom localStorage sd_last_read (fan pre-opened when it points at a\nsub-file). Clicks behave exactly like the old rows: reader.back = []\nthen openReaderPath with the same {list, idx} nav context, so\nPrev/Next still walks the path; leaf chips open their sub-file with\nthe module''s nav context.\n\nChips reuse the existing design system (glass tokens, radius-sm,\npointer spotlight via SPOT_SEL + section 16 selectors, ease-out motion,\nreduced-motion respected); the filter input dims non-matching nodes\n(opacity .25) so the path shape stays; chevrons carry aria-expanded\nand chips step-N-of-M aria-labels. Fix along the way: .leaf-fan''s\ndisplay:flex defeated the hidden attribute, so all fans rendered open\non first paint ([hidden] override added).\n\nVerified with node --check plus a headless-Chrome CDP run against the\nlive server: 52 llm nodes rendered, expand/collapse re-lays out and\ngrows/restores container height, leaf click opens the reader on\nrgb(0,0,0) with working Prev/Next, here/practiced markers assert,\nfilter dims 50/52 without removing nodes, daylight theme and 560px\nsingle-column screenshots inspected; zero console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1074b99b03f87fd8b4f9cf2e19de98fe4a414983","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/1074b99b03f87fd8b4f9cf2e19de98fe4a414983"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDYzOTEwY2YzMGQ0N2QwODkwNmQzZTRkNjEyZTVmN2IwMzc4ODE5MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4","sha":"62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4"}],"sha":"63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/63910cf30d47d08906d3e4d612e5f7b037881934"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:31:01Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:31:01Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): derive weighted module-relatedness graphs for the Learning Path\n\nbuild_graph.py emits graph/<section>.json for all 12 sections from two\nmeasurable signals only — no authored or hallucinated edges:\n  1. real markdown cross-links between modules (each link = a dependency\n     vote; section-index READMEs excluded as navigation, not prerequisites)\n  2. IDF-weighted lexical overlap of each module''s own Q&A corpus from\n     questions/<section>.json (same lexical family as extract.py)\n\nPairs are undirected with weight w (links dominate 0.7, lexical refines\n0.3, capped at each module''s 4 strongest); the app orients every edge\nforward along the curated STUDY_ORDER at render time, keeping the graph\nan acyclic DAG grounded in existing curation. Link-rich sections: spring\n(52 linked pairs), java (50), llm (50), cs_fundamentals (34); sections\nwith zero cross-links (database, book, lld) are lexical-only and render\nfaint. Consumed by the upcoming Learning Path graph view in Study mode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b043dc74005674737085b3af3bc24417c2fa40b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/b043dc74005674737085b3af3bc24417c2fa40b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDYyZTk5OWU2Mzg3NWJiNTVhZGUxNTYwYjQzMTdkMjEzYjVkMGUzYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c","sha":"47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c"}],"sha":"62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/62e999e63875bb55ade1560b4317d213b5d0e3c4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:21:47Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T13:21:47Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs(diagrams): appeal-first diagram policy — retire ASCII-first default\n\nOwner policy change: diagrams use the most visually appealing renderable\nform that conveys the information accurately. The Mermaid diagram family\n(flowchart, sequenceDiagram, stateDiagram-v2, xychart-beta, pie,\nquadrantChart, timeline, sankey-beta — all render on GitHub and in the\ngame reader) is preferred in study section files; ASCII remains only for\nconstraint grids/masks, alignment-critical layout maps, and vector\ngeometry that Mermaid cannot draw.\n\nUpdates the root CLAUDE.md Formatting Rules + Mermaid section (and notes\nthat the bar-chart / number-line visual-intuition archetypes now author\nas xychart-beta), and rewrites the /mermaid-diagrams skill''s decision\nchecklist into a topology -> diagram-type table.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e7cb8c985265654458c9a5dbc8a7c09593dc376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/5e7cb8c985265654458c9a5dbc8a7c09593dc376"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDQ3YTg4MzA0NmFhZjg3NjIzYWU0NjViNzY2MThlYzZkZTMxOWUwNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee","sha":"31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee"}],"sha":"47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/47a883046aaf87623ae465b76618ec6de319e05c"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T12:20:38Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T12:20:38Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): round 2 — graphics/usability layer + reader hard limits\n\nHard limits (user-set, now codified in new game/CLAUDE.md, linked from root\nCLAUDE.md): reader surface is pitch-black #000000 opaque in EVERY theme, and\nreader prose is #e6e6e6 (10% below full white). Daylight reader overrides\nremoved; verified via computed style on midnight + daylight.\n\nGraphics: pointer-spotlight on glass cards (--mx/--my radial), scroll-driven\nstaggered reveals (.rise — renamed after colliding with the quiz''s .reveal\npanel, which carries display:none), aurora-mesh pointer parallax fed through\nthe drift keyframes, brand/score gradient shimmer, staggered option dealing,\nfloating +XP particles (combo-multiplied amount), combo ripple shockwaves,\nboss-banner pulse, animated SVG score ring on results, heatmap cascade,\nmastery-bar shine sweep, topbar stat pop + flame flicker, View Transitions\nAPI cross-fades between screens, date eyebrow, tile mini mastery bars.\n\nUsability: post-round miss review (wrong + learned with correct answer and\ndive-deeper links), type-to-filter on topic picker + Study lists, \"?\"\nkeyboard-shortcuts overlay (+ footer link), mouse back/forward buttons\n(reader back-stack -> prev/next topic -> close; screen back elsewhere; never\naborts a live deck), reader reading-progress bar + persisted A-/A+ font\ncontrols + back-to-top, full-name hover tooltips on truncated sidebar/TOC\nentries, Study \"Continue reading\" card, difficulty chips + n/N counter.\n\nAll flows re-verified headless (CDP driver): zero console errors; reduced\nmotion respected throughout.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c40a688ee0d46af76508e66cbf6d0c7a03246ee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/c40a688ee0d46af76508e66cbf6d0c7a03246ee3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDMxYzZjMDE1NGQ3NDc3MGFmMWQxNDY3YmEwMDlhYThlODg3ZmEzZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb","sha":"97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb"}],"sha":"31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/31c6c0154d74770af1d1467ba009aa8e887fa3ee"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T11:58:58Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T11:58:58Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(game): visual overhaul — 4 glass themes, interactive diagrams, engine hardening\n\nVisual: token-driven design system in style.css — data-theme themes\n(Midnight/Aurora/Ember/Daylight) over an animated aurora-mesh + blueprint-grid\nbackdrop, glass surfaces (backdrop-filter), SF-style display type + monospace\ndata voice, unified buttons/motion, single-hue chart ramps, SVG icons, theme\npicker popover (+ ?theme= URL preview), screen-enter transitions.\n\nDiagrams: unified lightbox for Mermaid AND ASCII diagrams — drag-to-pan,\nzoom-toward-cursor (wheel/buttons/dblclick/keys), fit-to-viewport; inline\nMermaid node hover glow; copy button on every code fence. Reader prose is\ntheme-scoped; code/ASCII/Mermaid stay dark islands in every theme.\n\nEngine fixes (from a 5-dimension adversarially-verified audit):\n- extract.py: content-stable question ids (md5 of module|question) so\n  re-extracts no longer orphan SM-2 review state (existing reviews migrated);\n  deterministic walk/sort, in-module dedup, abbreviation-safe first sentence\n- app.js: reader-open keyboard fall-through, key-repeat deck auto-complete,\n  offline-session replay queue, dead resize grips (missing ''#''), DST-safe\n  heatmap, Mermaid CDN retry, stale combo multiplier, double-skip guard,\n  corrupt-localStorage boot, local history cap + section field\n- server.py: progress write lock, 400 on malformed sessions, history carries\n  section (revives pick_today anti-repeat), questions/* served no-cache for\n  304 revalidation instead of no-store re-downloads\n- a11y: aria-live announcements, per-screen focus management, aria-pressed\n  toggles, labeled progress dots, focus-visible, reduced-motion, contrast\n- .gitignore: guard against accidental ubuntu@* data drops in the web root\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbe980df4d3e0214461f36323ae08fac52dcabd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/bbe980df4d3e0214461f36323ae08fac52dcabd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDk3YmNjMzBlYzc0OWVjNDVkZDgzMmMzOGJjYTc5NTQ0ZjYzYmQ4YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2","sha":"4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2"}],"sha":"97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/97bcc30ec749ec45dd832c38bca79544f63bd8bb"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-02T05:58:54Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-02T05:58:54Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): Phase H continuation — 78 new Mermaid diagrams across 37 files\n\nNon-conservative pass converting all remaining ASCII flowchart bare-fences to\nMermaid across the full LLM section (agents, frameworks, multi-agent, fine-tuning,\nalignment, inference, safety, observability, ops, ecosystem).\n\nFiles converted (37):\n- agents_and_tool_use: agent_reliability, computer_use_and_browser_agents,\n  sandboxed_code_execution, tool_selection_at_scale\n- agentic_frameworks: crewai, dspy, framework_observability, google_adk,\n  langchain_and_lcel, langgraph\n- multi_agent_systems: agent_debate_and_consensus, agent_to_agent_protocols,\n  agentic_commerce_and_payments, chatdev_and_software_simulation,\n  magentic_one_and_autogen_v04, multi_agent_security, openai_swarm_and_handoffs,\n  orchestrator_worker_pattern\n- fine_tuning: domain_adaptation, instruction_tuning\n- alignment_and_rlhf: README (verifiable rewards pipeline)\n- inference_and_decoding: speculative_decoding\n- mixture_of_experts, vllm_deep_dive, multimodal_models, mechanistic_interpretability,\n  data_flywheels_and_continuous_learning, llm_security, safety_and_alignment,\n  code_generation, ai_applications, llm_ecosystem_and_landscape, llm_observability,\n  llm_ops_platforms, llm_routing_and_model_selection, token_economics_and_cost_optimization,\n  diffusion_language_models\n\nGrand total: 152 Mermaid fences across 83 files in llm/\nDiagram types used: flowchart TD/LR, sequenceDiagram\nAll fences: One-Dark classDef palette, curve:basis, dark theme, no bare [] in diamonds\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"fe260060732ecf81be203c2139f9a53b21562af8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/fe260060732ecf81be203c2139f9a53b21562af8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDRjZjFhNGM3MThjMDFmYmVhMzI2OWQwNjE3NjczMWJmZTMzMWE1ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52","sha":"02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52"}],"sha":"4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4cf1a4c718c01fbea3269d06176731bfe331a5f2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:22:29Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:22:29Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): Phase G — Safety, eval, ops, regulations (6 diagrams)\n\nguardrails_and_content_safety/README.md\n  - Guardrail Placement: User Input → Input Guardrails (PII/topic/\n    injection/toxicity) → block or pass → LLM → Output Guardrails →\n    replace or pass → User Output + Audit Log\n  - Parallel Guardrail Architecture: Input fans out to LLM (1–3 s),\n    Safety Classifier (50–200 ms), PII Detector (50–200 ms) → Merge\n    (suppress if unsafe); total latency = max of three paths\n\nevaluation_and_benchmarks/README.md\n  - Evaluation Pipeline: New Model → Automated Benchmarks (MMLU/\n    HumanEval/RAGAs/safety) → Regression Check (< 2% regression) →\n    Human Eval (1 000 queries + LLM-as-judge) → A/B Test (5%, 48h)\n    → Gradual Rollout / Investigate and Fix\n\nllm_testing_strategies/README.md\n  - CI/CD Evaluation Pipeline: PR → Static Checks (~$0) → Unit Tests\n    (< 1 min, ~$0, mocked LLM) → Regression Eval (200-example golden,\n    5–10 min, ~$2) → pass? → merge / fail PR; nightly Full Eval Suite\n    (1 000 ex., 30 min, ~$20) → Dashboard\n\nllm_routing_and_model_selection/README.md\n  - Cascade Pattern with Confidence Check: Query → Cheap Model →\n    confidence check → PASS exit OR FAIL → Mid-Tier → confidence\n    check → PASS exit OR FAIL → Frontier Model → Final Response\n\nai_regulations_and_compliance/README.md\n  - EU AI Act Compliance Decision Tree: EU users? → Yes → risk tier\n    (banned / high-risk / GPAI / limited / minimal); each tier shows\n    key obligations; \"No\" exits to other jurisdictions\n\nKept as ASCII: GDPR Art. 22 compliance path, NIST AI RMF cycle,\nfalse-positive management tables, benchmark contamination narrative,\nA/B testing methodology prose, quality feedback loop text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"f4b14a44a3c293cb8e58d175942b0fae73a4b449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/f4b14a44a3c293cb8e58d175942b0fae73a4b449"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDAyNjY3ODExZjc4OWQ3NjlkYzM3MmY0OTdmZWZlYWY2MDY4ZmJhNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25","sha":"a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25"}],"sha":"02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/02667811f789d769dc372f497fefeaf6068fba52"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:19:32Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:19:32Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): Phase F — Inference, serving, optimization (6 diagrams)\n\ninference_engines/README.md\n  - Engine Selection Decision Tree: hardware-type decision diamond\n    → Apple Silicon (Ollama/llama.cpp) · consumer NVIDIA (vLLM) ·\n    data-centre NVIDIA (TensorRT/vLLM/SGLang) · CPU (llama.cpp) ·\n    HuggingFace (TGI)\n\ndeployment_and_mlops/README.md\n  - Full LLM Production Stack: Client → Load Balancer → LLM Gateway\n    → vLLM / OpenAI / Embedding fan-out → GPU Pool → Monitoring Stack\n  - Deployment Pipeline with Canary Strategy: Dev → Staging → Shadow\n    Mode → Canary (1–5%, 24–48h monitoring, auto-rollback on breach)\n    → Gradual Ramp → Full Rollout\n\nknowledge_distillation_and_model_merging/README.md\n  - Knowledge Distillation Pipeline: Training Data → parallel Teacher\n    (frozen 70B) + Student (trainable 7B) → logits/T → KL divergence\n    (soft labels) + cross-entropy (hard labels) → α-weighted combined\n    loss → backprop Student update (cycle arrow)\n  - Model Merging Decision Tree: 2 models/same base → SLERP; 3+/same\n    → TIES/DARE+TIES; same model diff runs → Soups; create larger →\n    FrankenMerge; add/remove capability → Task Arithmetic\n\nsmall_language_models_and_edge_ai/README.md\n  - Quantization Flow for Edge Deployment: Original FP16 (7.2 GB) →\n    GPTQ/AWQ/GGUF quantisation step → INT4 model (2.4 GB, 2 weights/\n    byte + FP16 scale per 32 groups) → runtime dequantisation on-the-\n    fly per matmul (XNNPACK/Metal/Vulkan/Qualcomm HTP)\n\nKept as ASCII: vLLM box-drawing Scheduler/Executor architecture,\nKV-cache memory layout arithmetic blocks, sampling/decoding strategy\ncurves, continuous-batching timeline diagrams, prefix-cache radix tree,\nBlue-Green 2-column ASCII, Observability stack + cost breakdown tables.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"37582f8c3c06a23400038e996d6dd458108a09b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/37582f8c3c06a23400038e996d6dd458108a09b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGE1OTM0YjRiYWNjODdhYTQ4MGQxOTg5M2FkYTY4NTVhYmEyY2VlMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6","sha":"05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6"}],"sha":"a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a5934b4bacc87aa480d19893ada6855aba2cee25"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:16:22Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:16:22Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): Phase E — Frameworks, multi-agent, MCP (6 diagrams)\n\nagentic_frameworks/README.md\n  - LangGraph Stateful Agent Flow: START → agent_node → tool_call/\n    final_answer → tool_node (loop) / END\n\nagentic_frameworks/haystack.md\n  - Hybrid Retrieval Pipeline: Query fan-out → BM25 + Embedding\n    retrievers → DocumentJoiner (dedup) → SimilarityRanker → top-3\n    → PromptBuilder → Generator → Answer\n\nagentic_frameworks/litellm_routing.md\n  - Routing with Fallback: Request → Router → Attempt 1 (anthropic-\n    direct) → fallback 5xx → Attempt 2 (bedrock) → fallback → Attempt 3\n    (azure, last resort) → 200 OK or 503. Topology and virtual-key\n    budget sections remain ASCII.\n\nmulti_agent_systems/README.md\n  - Message Passing / Actor Model: User → Coordinator → Research →\n    result back → Coding → code back → Test → results back → Final\n    answer. Fan-out tree patterns (+-- style) left as ASCII.\n\nmcp_model_context_protocol/README.md\n  - JSON-RPC Message Flow: sequenceDiagram Client↔Server for\n    initialize → tools/list → resources/list → tools/call → shutdown\n  - Sampling Flow: sequenceDiagram Server→Client→LLM→Client→Server\n    showing server-initiated LLM call with user consent checkpoint\n\nKept as ASCII: §5.1 host/multi-server topology box, §5.3 JSON-RPC\nmessage anatomy (code blocks), orchestrator-worker/swarm fan-out\ntrees, ChatDev/MetaGPT role tables, agent communication JSON.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"325755cee0ebb00ae416e146a65d53349725a9d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/325755cee0ebb00ae416e146a65d53349725a9d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDA1ZjkzMzFkYmY2YWFjMjg4Y2ZiZGY4MWU1YWMwOGJjNzJjN2U1YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/e77b052b600de6938aaef94e5a5734e3597a76f1","sha":"e77b052b600de6938aaef94e5a5734e3597a76f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/e77b052b600de6938aaef94e5a5734e3597a76f1"}],"sha":"05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/05f9331dbf6aac288cfbdf81e5ac08bc72c7e5a6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/e77b052b600de6938aaef94e5a5734e3597a76f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:13:02Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T17:13:02Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): Phase D — Agents core (16 diagrams)\n\nagents_and_tool_use/README.md\n  - Agent Loop: Plan→Act→Observe→Reflect with done/loop decision\n  - Function Calling Flow: user msg → LLM reasoning → tool call →\n    app code → inject result → LLM second call → response\n\nagents_and_tool_use/function_calling_and_tool_design.md\n  - Function Calling Flow: 7-step sequential single-tool flow\n  - Parallel Tool Call Flow: LLM fans out two calls in one response\n    → parallel execution → merge → LLM second call\n\nagents_and_tool_use/react_and_reasoning_patterns.md\n  - ReAct Loop: Thought→Action→Observation→done? with STUCK/abort\n    edge for repeated or max-step violations\n\nagents_and_tool_use/reflexion_and_self_correction.md\n  - Reflexion Loop: Actor→Evaluator→Self-Reflector→EpisodicMemory\n    back to Actor (max 3 retries)\n  - Self-Refine Loop: LLM generate→feedback decision→refine→repeat\n\nagents_and_tool_use/plan_and_execute.md\n  - Two-Phase Architecture: Task→Planner(Opus)→Executor(mini, per\n    step)→validate/replan?→Synthesis→Output\n\nagentic_workflow_patterns/README.md\n  - Prompt Chaining: 3-step LLM chain with gate pass/fail edges\n  - Routing: classifier→3 routes (cheap/mid/expensive)\n  - Parallelization Sectioning: doc→4 chunks→parallel LLMs→merge\n  - Parallelization Voting: 5 parallel LLMs→majority vote\n  - Orchestrator-Workers: orchestrator→specialized workers→synthesizer\n  - Evaluator-Optimizer: generator↔evaluator loop, pass exits\n\ncoding_agents/README.md\n  - SWE-agent ACI Loop: Issue→LLM→ACI commands→sandbox→observation\n    →loop until submit or max iterations\n\nvoice_agents/README.md\n  - Pipeline Architecture: Mic→VAD→STT→LLM(streaming)→TTS→Speaker\n    (total latency 800–1500ms good case)\n\nKept as ASCII: Claude Code subagent fan-out tree (+-- style),\nCursor Composer diff preview linear flow, voice barge-in numbered\nsteps, turn detection threshold comparison, Reflexion Episode N\nside-by-side box diagram.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"7088362d65da90b63c887e7289cd2fdeb1db70f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/7088362d65da90b63c887e7289cd2fdeb1db70f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/e77b052b600de6938aaef94e5a5734e3597a76f1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/e77b052b600de6938aaef94e5a5734e3597a76f1","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGU3N2IwNTJiNjAwZGU2OTM4YWFlZjk0ZTVhNTczNGUzNTk3YTc2ZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/54fa3a8acd8d4fcc894afd28b9426116bdbcef95","sha":"54fa3a8acd8d4fcc894afd28b9426116bdbcef95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/54fa3a8acd8d4fcc894afd28b9426116bdbcef95"}],"sha":"e77b052b600de6938aaef