README.md\n  - Self-Instruct Pipeline: seeds → LLM generate → ROUGE filter → quality filter → pool loop\n  - Quality Filtering Pipeline: 1M raw → dedup → RM scoring → diversity → human spot-check\n\nKept as ASCII: NF4 vs INT4 number grid, ZeRO stages table, PPO mechanics formula,\nDPO/RLHF/SimPO/GRPO side-by-side text comparison, double-quantisation arithmetic.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"dd3ee0d088d207f58ed37a91dd49fbe125581222","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/dd3ee0d088d207f58ed37a91dd49fbe125581222"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/134d9f393a99a789ca24b5a60037f472390a4b65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/134d9f393a99a789ca24b5a60037f472390a4b65","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDEzNGQ5ZjM5M2E5OWE3ODljYTI0YjVhNjAwMzdmNDcyMzkwYTRiNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef","sha":"12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef"}],"sha":"134d9f393a99a789ca24b5a60037f472390a4b65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/134d9f393a99a789ca24b5a60037f472390a4b65"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:59:13Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:59:13Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm/mermaid): Phase A — Foundations & representation (7 diagrams)\n\nConvert true directed flowcharts; leave grids/curves/tensor-shape blocks as ASCII.\n\nfoundations_and_architecture/README.md\n  - Multi-Head Attention Detail: Q/K/V fan-out → attention → concat → output\n  - MoE Routing: router → softmax → top-K expert fan-out → weighted sum\n\nfoundations_and_architecture/state_space_models_and_linear_attention.md\n  - Selective SSM Block (Mamba): x_t 3-way fan-out → delta/B/C → state h_t → y_t\n\ntokenization_and_embeddings/README.md\n  - Tokenization Pipeline: Raw Text → Normalize → Pre-tokenize → Encode → ID → Embed\n\nembeddings_and_similarity_search/README.md\n  - Embedding Retrieval Pipeline: Query → bi-encoder → ANN → fetch → cross-encoder rerank → LLM\n\npre_training/README.md\n  - Pre-Training Data Pipeline: 5 sources → dedup → quality-filter → mix → pack → train\n\ntraining_infrastructure/README.md\n  - Data Parallelism: 4 GPUs → AllReduce → update all model copies\n\nKept as ASCII: causal mask grid, softmax temperature bar chart, MHA/GQA/MQA head-sharing\ncomparison, Pre-LN/Post-LN side-by-side, tensor-shape walkthrough, RoPE rotation math,\nALiBi bias grid, \"lost in the middle\" curve, ZeRO stage table, memory budget tables.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"14fdfdbe4cdb908328bdf244df1e71e65b29d705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/14fdfdbe4cdb908328bdf244df1e71e65b29d705"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDEyZDViMzUyOTk5ZmU2MDU3YzZkNDkwNmVlMjk3ZTM2NmU1MTM4ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075","sha":"346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075"}],"sha":"12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/12d5b352999fe6057c6d4906ee297e366e5138ef"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:25:39Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:25:39Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix(reader): strip stray colon from md-qa and definition-list md-a paragraphs\n\nTwo patterns left a lone \":\" visible after the display:block Q/A change:\n\n1. md-qa — \"**Label**: answer text\" rendered as <strong>Label</strong>: answer,\n   then display:block made strong take a full line and \": answer\" appeared below.\n   Fix: strip the \":\" immediately after the closing ** before rendering.\n\n2. md-a — Markdown definition-list format (**Term**\\n: definition) puts a literal\n   \": \" at the start of the answer paragraph. Fix: strip leading \": \" from md-a\n   paragraphs (this is always a definition-list separator, never meaningful content).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"cbe428fa8312cb36ecdb624922edaf616005e57d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/cbe428fa8312cb36ecdb624922edaf616005e57d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDM0NjAwMWI0OTkxNzE5MDlkOTlkNjc3NjFiZjM3NjExNTc3NjAwNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679","sha":"d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679"}],"sha":"346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/346001b499171909d99d67761bf3761157760075"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:06:05Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T16:06:05Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs(skill): update mermaid-diagrams skill with [bracket] syntax trap + zoom\n\nTwo new Gotchas entries:\n- [...]  square brackets in node labels: Mermaid v11 lexer interprets bare [text]\n  as a rect-node shape token even inside {} / ([]) shapes; fix = quote the full\n  label or replace [ ] with ( ); includes confirmed version (11.16.0)\n- Click-to-zoom: documents that renderMermaid() wires zoom globally — no\n  per-diagram work needed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"90ec8915e9daae167e697660750e75d78aed2e77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/90ec8915e9daae167e697660750e75d78aed2e77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGQ3ZWJkZWE0Y2E0MDhmMDYyNTA2MDcyYzNlZjZiZTgwNGI2ZWM2Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19","sha":"0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19"}],"sha":"d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/d7ebdea4ca408f062506072c3ef6be804b6ec679"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T15:03:09Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T15:03:09Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"Game Hyperlink","tree":{"sha":"67a6daf06e0e7fa8f23d6e380662241fd078a83a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/67a6daf06e0e7fa8f23d6e380662241fd078a83a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBlYzZiN2Y0OTFjYTk3MzljYzdlM2EwNGM0OWYzNjU5ZDhjYmJhMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615","sha":"a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615"}],"sha":"0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0ec6b7f491ca9739cc7e3a04c49f3659d8cbba19"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T15:01:26Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T15:01:26Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix + feat: Mermaid syntax errors, diagram click-to-zoom\n\nSyntax fixes:\n- corrective_rag.md: RE{...score each doc [0.0–1.0]...} → RE{\"...(0.0–1.0)...\"}\n  Bare [ ] inside a {} diamond label parse as node-shape syntax in Mermaid v11\n- self_rag.md: DEC{[Retrieve] token...} same fix; also removed [ ] from node labels\n  inside rect[\"...\"] shapes that contained [Relevant]/[Irrelevant] references\n\nDiagram zoom (app.js + style.css):\n- Click any Mermaid diagram to open a full-screen dark overlay with the SVG\n- Overlay controls: − (zoom out 25%), % label, + (zoom in 25%), ↺ (reset 100%), ✕ (close)\n- Mouse-wheel zoom inside the overlay box (10% per notch, passive:false)\n- Close on: ✕ button, Escape key, or clicking the dark background\n- Hover hint: faint \"⤢ zoom\" label in top-right corner of every diagram (cursor:zoom-in)\n- CSS vars + One-Dark palette so the overlay matches the reader theme\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"b9ec771943374bd678c52bd1aeea07ba8b04d5ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/b9ec771943374bd678c52bd1aeea07ba8b04d5ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGE1YzUxMGRjYmQxZjRmMGUzYTM2YjhlOWM5NjYyMGQwODA3Y2U2MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845","sha":"b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845"}],"sha":"a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a5c510dcbd1f4f0e3a36b8e9c96620d0807ce615"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T14:50:17Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T14:50:17Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat(llm): Mermaid diagrams for rag_fundamentals + advanced_rag (15 diagrams)\n\nConverts all true pipeline/decision-flow ASCII blocks to One-Dark Mermaid\nacross 10 files; visual-intuition diagrams (grids, text comparisons, embedding\nspace sketches) intentionally kept as ASCII per the mermaid-diagrams skill rules.\n\nrag_fundamentals/README.md (3):\n  Standard RAG Pipeline · Indexing Pipeline · Query Routing (Multi-Source)\n\nrag_fundamentals/reranking.md (1):\n  Two-Stage Retrieval Pipeline\n\nrag_fundamentals/retrieval_methods.md (1):\n  Hybrid Retrieval Pipeline (parallel dense+sparse paths → RRF → rerank)\n\nadvanced_rag/README.md (2):\n  Agentic RAG with Reflection · Graph RAG Architecture (combined indexing+query)\n\nadvanced_rag/agentic_rag.md (1):\n  Agentic RAG Control Flow (full loop with max-iter fallback to best-effort)\n\nadvanced_rag/corrective_rag.md (1):\n  CRAG Decision Flow (3-branch: CORRECT / MIXED / INCORRECT)\n\nadvanced_rag/graph_rag.md (2):\n  Graph RAG Indexing Pipeline · Graph RAG Query Pipeline (GLOBAL/LOCAL branches)\n\nadvanced_rag/multimodal_rag.md (2):\n  Multimodal Indexing Pipeline (text/table/figure fan-out) ·\n  Multimodal Query Pipeline (text+image parallel retrieval paths)\n\nadvanced_rag/query_transformation.md (1):\n  Query Transformation Pipeline (4-branch: rewrite/HyDE/multi-query/decompose)\n\nadvanced_rag/self_rag.md (1):\n  Self-RAG Token Generation Flow ([Retrieve] vs [No Retrieve] decision)\n\nEvery fence: %%{init curve:basis}%%, One-Dark palette (io/proc/llm/store/decide/\nsearch/warn classDefs), class assignments at bottom after subgraph ends.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"fcd5f56e963df3ca4cb459ed0654bf160b80ea1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/fcd5f56e963df3ca4cb459ed0654bf160b80ea1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGIxMjMwOWUxOTUyNzIzYjM3YmI3YzBiM2MxOWMwODlhMTVlYTg4NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a","sha":"89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a"}],"sha":"b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/b12309e1952723b37bb7c0b3c19c089a15ea8845"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:31:24Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:31:24Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"fix: Mermaid smooth curves on GitHub, thicker arrows, Q&A on separate lines\n\nMermaid init directives (lora.md):\n- Add %%{init: {''flowchart'': {''curve'': ''basis'', ...}}}%% to all 4 diagrams;\n  this embeds the smoothing config in the diagram source itself so GitHub''s\n  native Mermaid renderer picks it up — previously only the game reader set\n  curve:''basis'' via mermaid.initialize(), which GitHub does not honour\n\nArrow + edge polish (style.css):\n- stroke-width: 2.5px → 3px + added stroke-linejoin:round to reduce\n  corner aliasing stairstepping at low DPI (the linecap:round was already set)\n\nQ&A reader layout (style.css):\n- p.md-qa > strong:first-child: display:block so inline **Question?** Answer\n  splits into two lines (question yellow, answer below)\n- p.md-a margin-top: 2px so the answer paragraph sits tight under its\n  paired md-q question, rather than floating with default paragraph spacing\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"f76e74e5cfe83be6e21c9e62d95d91621e612354","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/f76e74e5cfe83be6e21c9e62d95d91621e612354"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDg5YWE2NWZkN2Q4MDE5ZjYzZWQxNzg1MzBlNjA3MWVmYTI1MWI0MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e","sha":"9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e"}],"sha":"89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/89aa65fd7d8019f63ed178530e6071efa251b40a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:24:40Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:24:40Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"feat: resizable left+right sidebars, brighter reader text, thicker Mermaid arrows\n\nSidebar resize (app.js + style.css):\n- CSS variables --modules-w:160px and --toc-w:190px replace fixed sidebar widths\n  so they can be updated live via drag\n- .modules-grip and .toc-grip: 8px drag handles (col-resize cursor) between\n  reader-modules↔readerMain and readerMain↔reader-toc; hidden when their sidebar\n  is hidden; highlight to --accent on hover / during drag (same visual as the\n  existing reader-grip)\n- attachGrip() generalized: accepts onMove(ev) and onDone() callbacks so the\n  pointer-capture boilerplate is shared across all three grips\n- wireGrips() wires #readerGrip (outer shell, available at panel build time);\n  wireSidebarGrips() wires #modulesGrip and #tocGrip separately — called after\n  b.innerHTML is set so the elements exist in the DOM; both called per-navigation\n- restoreReaderWidth() restores sd_modules_w and sd_toc_w from localStorage\n  alongside sd_reader_w so sidebar widths persist across sessions\n- Mermaid SVGs reflow automatically (max-width:100% + flex: 1 1 auto on main)\n\nVisual fixes:\n- --od-text: #abb2bf → #c5cad6 (noticeably brighter body text without harsh contrast\n  of full white; improves legibility on pitch-black background)\n- Mermaid arrow stroke-width: 2px → 2.5px + stroke-linecap:round to reduce\n  aliasing stairstepping on low-res / non-retina monitors\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"83c20f7789b33627284db3061b8324cd0c516af2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/83c20f7789b33627284db3061b8324cd0c516af2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDljYWMyMjJlZGFjNGU1Yzg3NjgxMTE3NTczOTdkODVjMWExNjk5NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d","sha":"c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d"}],"sha":"9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/9cac222edac4e5c8768111757397d85c1a16994e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:17:05Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:17:05Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"docs: update mermaid-diagrams skill + CLAUDE.md with post-processing knowledge\n\nskill/mermaid-diagrams/SKILL.md:\n- New \"Reader Rendering Architecture\" section documents exactly what renderMermaid()\n  does and WHY three things require JS post-processing (corner radius, arrowhead\n  marker color, edge label background) — the root causes are architectural SVG\n  constraints, not Mermaid bugs, so future edits don''t need per-diagram workarounds\n- Full post-processing code block (rx=8 on .node rect, rx=12 on .cluster rect,\n  fill=#61afef on marker path/polygon) + full CSS override block for reference\n- Explains why edgeLabelBackground:\"transparent\" is correct (default \"#000000\"\n  paints a visible pill on dark backgrounds)\n- Gotchas reordered: three new root-cause entries (grey arrowheads, black pill,\n  square nodes) placed first because they are the most likely confusion points;\n  existing Mermaid syntax gotchas follow\n\nCLAUDE.md — Mermaid Diagrams section:\n- Added paragraph explaining that post-processing is already wired globally in\n  renderMermaid(); per-diagram workarounds are not needed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"b13376f792df2090a9811a1ba859aaf62ed82336","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/b13376f792df2090a9811a1ba859aaf62ed82336"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGM3ZGRlMjRlZjZiMTgxNzY1OTU3NDI4NmRmYjdiNDA3MWI5NGVmOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9","sha":"2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9"}],"sha":"c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/c7dde24ef6b1817659574286dfb7b4071b94ef9d"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:10:37Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T12:10:37Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"polish: Mermaid diagrams — rounded nodes, blue arrows, clean edge labels\n\napp.js — renderMermaid() improvements:\n- themeVariables: edgeLabelBackground → transparent (removes the black pill\n  that was appearing around \"× alpha/r\" and gradient labels)\n- themeVariables: clusterBkg/clusterBorder updated to subtle blue-tinted rgba\n  values so subgraph boxes look intentional, not like a debug rectangle\n- flowchart config: curve:\"basis\" for smooth bezier curves; nodeSpacing:45,\n  rankSpacing:55 for better breathing room\n- SVG post-processing after mermaid.run(): sets rx=8/ry=8 on all .node rect\n  elements (Mermaid does not expose a corner-radius themeVariable), sets rx=12\n  on .cluster rect for rounded subgraph boxes, and recolors all <marker>\n  elements to #61afef (arrowhead markers are separate SVG defs that ignore\n  the lineColor themeVariable — this was the root cause of grey arrowheads)\n\nstyle.css additions:\n- .edgePath .path — stroke:#61afef 2px (belt+suspenders with JS marker fix)\n- .edgeLabel .label rect — fill:transparent so no rect shows behind label text\n- .edgeLabel foreignObject > div — transparent background, gold text color\n- .cluster rect — stroke-dasharray:5 3, stroke-width:1.5 for dashed subgraph\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"dc24f57b4bc45e1cc34220b062ec58a068d9e435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/dc24f57b4bc45e1cc34220b062ec58a068d9e435"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDJiMTlmYjI2ZjIxOTRmNWFmNzkyMTQ5MWI5ZmRhZmFjNDE1YWFjYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1","sha":"a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1"}],"sha":"2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/2b19fb26f2194f5af7921491b9fdafac415aaca9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T11:36:53Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T11:36:53Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"add /mermaid-diagrams skill + update CLAUDE.md diagram rules\n\nNew skill at .claude/skills/mermaid-diagrams/SKILL.md:\n- Decision checklist: Mermaid vs ASCII (grids/bar charts/deltas stay ASCII;\n  directed flowcharts with many branches or crossing arrows use Mermaid)\n- Full One-Dark classDef block: io/frozen/train/mathOp/lossN/req/base (colors\n  proven working in lora.md experiment with confirmed SVG classDef rendering)\n- Diagram type selection: flowchart LR vs TD vs sequenceDiagram\n- ASCII → Mermaid 6-step conversion guide (topology extract → class assign →\n  write fence → verify reader → delete ASCII → leave adjacent grids alone)\n- Node shape reference, edge style conventions (solid=forward, dotted=gradient)\n- Gotchas: classDef order, data-processed removal, esc() round-trip safety,\n  stale readerCache fix, subgraph title quoting\n\nCLAUDE.md changes:\n- Formatting Rules: ASCII-first rule updated to document the Mermaid exception\n  (directed flowcharts only, in study section files, via /mermaid-diagrams skill)\n- New \"Mermaid Diagrams\" section at end: when to invoke the skill, which files\n  are in scope, how the reader + GitHub both render mermaid fences\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"062190955e6fd7b240edadf99ee57ac1f3a53111","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/062190955e6fd7b240edadf99ee57ac1f3a53111"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGE0OGUzZGM1MmM2ODI4Zjk2ZmEyOWJjODU1MGY4YTU1MmI1MWVmYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0","sha":"4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0"}],"sha":"a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a48e3dc52c6828f96fa29bc8550f8a552b51efc1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T11:30:27Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T11:30:27Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"experiment: Mermaid diagrams in lora.md + reader Mermaid support\n\nConverts 4 ASCII flowcharts in llm/fine_tuning/lora.md to colorful Mermaid\ndiagrams (intentional exception to the repo ASCII-only rule for this one file).\nColor-codes nodes by semantic role via classDef: blue = I/O tensors, green =\ntrainable matrices (A, B), purple = frozen weights (W), orange = math ops (+),\nred = Loss, teal = requests, gold = base model, yellow = adapters.\n\ngame/ reader changes:\n- mdRender: mermaid fence → <div class=\"mermaid\"> (before highlighter checks)\n- renderMermaid(): lazy import of mermaid@11 ESM from jsDelivr CDN; only\n  fetched when a page actually has .mermaid divs; try/catch so CDN failure\n  leaves raw source visible instead of crashing; called after wireReaderBody\n- themeVariables: bright blue edges, gold subgraph titles, near-black cluster\n  bg, monospace font\n- style.css: .md-body .mermaid border + padding + svg max-width:100%\n\nDebug note: classDef works correctly via innerHTML path (esc() → &quot; →\ntextContent decodes back to \"); stale readerCache was the reason first render\nshowed grey nodes — cleared with delete readerCache[path] before reload.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"f14bccd2abe185fbec5b958a7ecf3f4bbcd4231c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/f14bccd2abe185fbec5b958a7ecf3f4bbcd4231c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDQ2ODVmYjY5MDJmNTFmNTNmMWNmMTdjYjJkYTAxM2I2OWE0MjcxYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f","sha":"a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f"}],"sha":"4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4685fb6902f51f53f1cf17cb2da013b69a4271b0"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T10:28:34Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T10:28:34Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"game: dual-sidebar reader (module tree + TOC) + pitch-black theme\n\nLeft sidebar: VS Code-style file tree — single-file modules as plain\nlinks, multi-file modules as collapsible folders (▶/▼) with sub-files\nlisted; auto-expands the active module; session-persistent expand state.\nextract.py now emits a \\\"files\\\" map in questions/index.json (374 modules,\n30 with sub-files) so the tree builds without extra server roundtrips.\n\nRight sidebar: file-content TOC (existing, moved to right side in this\nsession). Both independently toggleable and localStorage-persistent.\n\nReader backgrounds: --od-bg #000000, --od-bg2 #080808, --od-line #1a1a1a\n(was #282c34 / #21252b / #3b4048 One Dark grey). Hardcoded #2c313a code\nand table-header backgrounds replaced with #111111.\n\nModule names now capitalize via CSS (moduleName is lowercase in bank).\nSidebar scrollbars hidden (scrollbar-width:none + ::-webkit-scrollbar).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"868683fcffb2fa8d069954553141761f213a0b93","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/868683fcffb2fa8d069954553141761f213a0b93"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKGE3MGUxZDczN2E3OTAxM2I4NWFlNDM2ODQ5NjM4MDA3YzBlODkwMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52","sha":"4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52"}],"sha":"a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/a70e1d737a79013b85ae436849638007c0e8902f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T12:18:56Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T12:18:56Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"game: phase-ordered Study mode + pitch-black theme; standardise README learning paths\n\ngame/app.js:\n- STUDY_ORDER: 12-section phase map (all 200+ modules in canonical learning order)\n- modulesOf: sort by STUDY_ORDER index instead of alphabetically; unregistered modules\n  fall to the end so future additions degrade gracefully\n\ngame/style.css:\n- Background: #0f1320 navy → #000000 pitch black; remove coloured gradient\n- Cards: #1d2438 → #111111; accent/good/bad secondary vars adjusted accordingly\n\nREADME standardisation:\n- cs_fundamentals: \"6-Phase Learning Path\" → \"5-Phase\" (actual content is 5 phases)\n- devops: \"7-Phase Learning Path\" → \"8-Phase\" (Phase 8 was added without updating heading)\n- java: \"6-Phase Learning Path\" → \"8-Phase\"; reorder 24-row module table by phase\n  (strings, generics, exceptions moved to Phase 1; design_patterns to Phase 4 group;\n   annotation_processing to Phase 6; Phase 7-8 modules in order)\n- spring: reorder 32-row module table by phase (spring_modulith → Phase 3 row 10;\n  spring_graphql + validation_and_error_handling → Phase 4; spring_batch/events/ai/\n  integration contiguous in Phase 7; observability/native_graalvm contiguous in Phase 8)\n- hld: add consensus_algorithms and event_sourcing_cqrs to Phase 3 learning path\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"e41c6a00ab4f8ccfbc9b43d05decad82d4c648d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/e41c6a00ab4f8ccfbc9b43d05decad82d4c648d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDRiMTQxNWJkMDAyYTdjNDc4YWZkOTg3NDJiYWRkNjIwOTVjZGRjNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a","sha":"95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a"}],"sha":"4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/4b1415bd002a7c478afd98742badd62095cddc52"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:47:23Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:47:23Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"ci: GitHub Actions Pages deploy + short /game/ URL redirect\n\n- .github/workflows/pages.yml: on every push to main, runs extract.py fresh\n  so newly added modules auto-populate the question bank without a manual rebuild;\n  deploys the whole repo as the Pages artifact (no committed questions/*.json needed)\n- game/index.html (repo root): rppol.github.io/system-design/game/ bounces to game\n- index.html (repo root): rppol.github.io/system-design/ also bounces to game\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"27363e18029c8bc89854d839ba29f695e46be1de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/27363e18029c8bc89854d839ba29f695e46be1de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDk1YmJjNWE5NTU2NGFlNGE5MjEyZWExYzkxYzk1YTcwOGFjZTUxM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f","sha":"73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f"}],"sha":"95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/95bbc5a95564ae4a9212ea1c91c95a708ace513a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:45:49Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:45:49Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"game: GitHub Pages support — static hosting with localStorage persistence\n\n- IS_STATIC auto-detects non-local hostnames (github.io / any non-loopback);\n  on GitHub Pages: no /api/ calls, progress is fully browser-localStorage-based\n- Port SM-2 scheduleReview() from server.py to JS; add per-question review\n  scheduling to saveSessionLocal (was missing — offline fallback was incomplete)\n- Content fetch uses relative path (../<path>) on static, /content/<path> locally\n- Skip /api/today on static (falls back to deterministic section picker already in JS)\n- Root index.html redirect: rppol.github.io/system-design/ → game/\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"3e765010ee126e9877856ab333c9d67dd33399f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/3e765010ee126e9877856ab333c9d67dd33399f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDczYzZjMTA4MGRkYTg5YWViZjkwNGZhZDgzZmYzOGRhYjg1ZjViOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165","sha":"0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165"}],"sha":"73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/73c6c1080dda89aebf904fad83ff38dab85f5b9f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:41:07Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-30T08:41:07Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"game/reader: One Dark renderer, Study mode, syntax highlight, fullscreen, TOC, cross-links\n\n- Hand-rolled zero-dep tokenizer (java/python/sql/yaml/bash/json/js/dockerfile/properties)\n  with One Dark palette; fences with unrecognized tags render verbatim (diagram safety)\n- Alignment-safe ASCII diagram colouring — wrap chars only, never alter, round-trip proven\n- Semantic Markdown colours: h1 red, h2 blue, h3 purple, h4 teal; questions yellow,\n  answers muted; inline-bold Q+A paragraphs get md-qa class\n- Study mode: top-bar button → section grid → module list → reader with Prev/Next nav\n- Reader fullscreen (F key / ⛶ button) + always-accessible collapsible sidebar TOC (☰)\n- Drag-resizable left edge with localStorage persistence; width survives reload\n- Working cross-links: relative .md links open in-reader with a Back button;\n  in-page anchors + TOC scroll within the pane; external links open new tab\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F6xS6LLRRK9KC9Kyt5AFzA","tree":{"sha":"bfe02b1f3e19788bf8696a7ae0e5381a22c886b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/bfe02b1f3e19788bf8696a7ae0e5381a22c886b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDBhNzA3Y2I1NTg2ZDJhZmE2MTQ1MTY4NWNhNzQwNDYxZmJjZGUxNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5","sha":"721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5"}],"sha":"0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/0a707cb5586d2afa61451685ca740461fbcde165"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-29T07:33:34Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-29T07:33:34Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"Add game/ section: daily learning game with engagement + learning features\n\nIntroduces the browser-based daily learning game (zero-dependency vanilla-JS\nSPA + stdlib server.py + extract.py question bank) and a first wave of\nengagement and learning features built on it:\n\n- Streak freeze/grace: banked tokens auto-cover a single missed day; one\n  re-earned per 7-day milestone (cap 3), same-day-replay farming guarded.\n- Activity heatmap: GitHub-style contribution grid from the history array.\n- Drill weak spots: deck from lowest-accuracy sections, prioritising lapses.\n- In-app split-view reader: dependency-free Markdown renderer; fenced blocks\n  render verbatim in <pre> so the ASCII diagrams keep alignment.\n- Flashcard self-grade mode (top-bar Quiz/Cards toggle); feeds the same SM-2\n  schedule as the blitz, with flat XP so it can''t inflate score.\n- Mastery tiers (Bronze/Silver/Gold) + global level chip; mastery-decay nudge.\n\nServer: backfill new progress fields on read (ensure_fields); per-section\nlastPlayed; no-store on all responses so the zero-build SPA is never stale.\n\nRoot CLAUDE.md/README.md: register the game/ section.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fac76aae7ebcc8b38cbb1e6bbdad600231fc6e92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/fac76aae7ebcc8b38cbb1e6bbdad600231fc6e92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDcyMTU0Njg2MTc3M2JlZjJlNGY3ZDMzZGYyNDdjYzExODYyZDZmYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13","sha":"99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13"}],"sha":"721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/721546861773bef2e4f7d33df247cc11862d6fa5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-23T08:25:58Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-23T08:25:58Z","email":"rutikp@finfactor.ai","name":"rutik46"},"message":"Add Book section: Designing Data-Intensive Applications summary\n\nNew top-level book/ section (alongside hld/lld/database/etc.) holding\nchapter-by-chapter book summaries, organized by book then chapter.\n\nFirst book: Designing Data-Intensive Applications (Kleppmann) — preface\n+ all 12 chapters, each faithful to the book''s own section order so the\nsection reads as a standalone replacement for the book and cross-links\nback into the repo''s database/hld deep dives.\n\n- New book-faithful chapter template (not the 14-section module template),\n  documented in book/CLAUDE.md\n- Per-chapter: ASCII diagrams (validator-clean), key-concept glossary,\n  tradeoff tables, war stories, 15+ interview Q&As, repo cross-links\n- Build manifest in the DDIA index README (all 13 files done)\n- Registered in root README.md and root CLAUDE.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e83e85d54174a51559471ecb4184572364ed4999","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/trees/e83e85d54174a51559471ecb4184572364ed4999"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/git/commits/99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13","node_id":"C_kwDOSY0T1NoAKDk5ZTZiZGJlM2M3ZTQzMmJjZjhkNmUyN2U4MzZjYjJlMTE4NzdmMTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rppol/system-design/commit/1525feb56a36fe3d04b01f342078685f3b40f9ef","sha":"1525feb56a36fe3d04b01f342078685f3b40f9ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/1525feb56a36fe3d04b01f342078685f3b40f9ef"}],"sha":"99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rppol/system-design/commits/99e6bdbe3c7e432bcf8d6e27e836cb2e11877f13"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/