aniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_docs: ship capstone doc pass reconciling design docs with solo-prep reality\n\nAll solo-prep predecessor tasks are complete (ADR 0049 + sp_adr through sp_e2e).\nThis pass promotes the five canonical docs from planning-era framing to shipped\nreality, per tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_docs.md.\n\n- docs/solo-prep.md — status banner → Shipped (M13 + ADR 0049); entry-point now boolean `solo` flag + \"Just me — solo prep\" checkbox + \"Solo prep\" badge; all three Open Questions closed as resolved\n- DESIGN.md — doc-index entry and prep-workflow open-question both record solo prep as shipped (M13, ADR 0049)\n- docs/architecture.md — #scope-v1 now includes Solo Prep; role-conflation note extended with host == moderator == sole position-holder step\n- docs/moderator-ui.md — new \"Solo prep console\" section (visible-but-pre-satisfied vote/commit + operator-holds-position)\n- docs/methodology.md — agreement-rule section and \"no special cases\" line amended for party-of-one case, citing ADR 0049\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — complete 100 on sp_docs\n- tasks/99-milestones.tji — complete 100 on m_solo_prep (M13); all dependencies confirmed complete\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_docs.md — Status block appended\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see logs):\n  - check: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0013-verify-check.log)\n  - vitest: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0013-verify-vitest.log)\n  - cucumber: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0013-verify-cucumber.log)\n  - playwright: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0013-verify-playwright.log)\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"16fe7f1f83e2e61d906a3abafbff0f8e2466b5c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/16fe7f1f83e2e61d906a3abafbff0f8e2466b5c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/31d64c6ed757450dac47e9983fc28c6d1ca3e2c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/31d64c6ed757450dac47e9983fc28c6d1ca3e2c7","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDMxZDY0YzZlZDc1NzQ1MGRhYzQ3ZTk5ODNmYzI4YzZkMWNhM2UyYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c","sha":"56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c"}],"sha":"31d64c6ed757450dac47e9983fc28c6d1ca3e2c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/31d64c6ed757450dac47e9983fc28c6d1ca3e2c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T10:20:48Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T10:20:48Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"moderator_ui.mod_graph_rendering.xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render_edge_annotation: ship cited cross-session edge/annotation rendering on the destination moderator canvas\n\nCloses the client-side gap for cross-session cited edges and annotations. The\nxsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader task (2026-06-15) made the\nserver projection correct — resolving borrowed edges/annotations and their full\nFK closure into BorrowedEntities — but the moderator canvas still rendered from\nthe WS event log, which had no entity-included arm for edges or annotations.\n\nThis task generalizes the node-canvas sidecar seam (xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render)\nto the full set of borrowable entity kinds. The wire schema''s singular\nborrowedNode? field becomes a borrowedEntities? closure (nodes/edges/annotations);\nbuildEventAppliedFrame now attaches the FK closure for entity-included{edge} and\nentity-included{annotation} events; the shell store carries per-kind maps; and\nselectEdgesForSession / projectModeratorAnnotations gain entity-included arms that\nrender borrowed edges/annotations through the existing StatementEdge /\nAnnotationBadge components.\n\nA fixer pass resolved a timing regression in solo-prep-flow.spec.ts (layout-settle\nbefore tidy-up + ensureHandlesInViewport zoom-out after tidy-up), and a second\nfixer pass corrected the solo-session commit-gate bug where deriveAllAgree returned\nno-current-participants for a vacuously-satisfied solo set, disabling the annotate\nbutton.\n\n- packages/shared-types/src/ws-envelope.ts (+.test.ts): generalize borrowedNode? → borrowedEntities? closure schema\n- apps/server/src/ws/broadcast/event-applied-frame.ts (+.test.ts): attach FK closure for edge/annotation entity-included events\n- packages/shell/src/ws/store-contract.ts, defaultStore.ts (+.test.ts), client.ts: add borrowedEdgeContent/borrowedAnnotationContent maps; applyEvent(event, borrowedEntities?)\n- apps/moderator/src/graph/selectors.ts (+.test.ts): entity-included{edge} arm in selectEdgesForSession; borrowed-annotation arm in projectModeratorAnnotations\n- apps/moderator/src/graph/GraphCanvasPane.tsx (+.test.tsx): emitBorrowedNode for endpoint/target nodes; thread borrowed maps at all 3 call sites\n- apps/moderator/src/graph/proposalFacets.ts (+.test.ts): solo corollary to deriveAllAgree; canonical deriveSessionSolo\n- apps/moderator/src/graph/proposalFilter.ts: thread solo into the Ready-chip gate\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/PendingProposalsPane.tsx: derive solo from events, thread to row gate + filter\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/useProposalCommitChord.ts: thread solo into chord gate\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/AxiomMarkSubmenu.tsx: re-export deriveSessionSolo from its new home\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/CaptureTargetChip.test.tsx, apps/participant/src/proposals/useNewProposalArrival.test.ts: session-state literals updated for new required fields\n- tests/behavior/backend/ws-catch-up.feature + steps: new cited-edge/annotation closure scenario; node assertion migrated to borrowedEntities.nodes\n- tests/e2e/solo-prep-flow.spec.ts: draw edge + commit annotation in source, cite both, assert graph-edge-label-<id> / statement-node-<id> / annotation-badge-<id> on destination console\n- tasks/30-moderator-ui.tji: complete 100 on xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render_edge_annotation\n- tasks/refinements/moderator-ui/xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render_edge_annotation.md: Status block appended\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"924ac338e8f3ffaeb20ac9753bd3d655b8292180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/924ac338e8f3ffaeb20ac9753bd3d655b8292180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDU2ZGNhMzYyMjlmYzIzNTI2YWJkOWZjOGU3YjQ5OTIwYWE3M2NlMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f","sha":"6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f"}],"sha":"56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/56dca36229fc23526abd9fc8e7b49920aa73ce0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T07:11:42Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T07:11:42Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"moderator_ui.mod_graph_rendering.xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render: ship cited cross-session node rendering on the destination moderator canvas\n\nCloses the client gap that kept borrowed (cross-session cited) nodes invisible\non the destination operate console. The server-side projection was already\ncorrect (xsession_inclusion_render_loader, 2026-06-15); this task delivers the\nborrowed node''s resolved wording to the moderator client over the WS stream and\nteaches projectNodes to render it through the existing StatementNode component.\n\nWire schema: `event-applied` payload gains an optional `borrowedNode` sidecar\n(packages/shared-types/src/ws-envelope.ts) so the resolved wording travels with\nthe `entity-included` event frame — additive and optional so existing clients\nare unaffected. A shared `buildEventAppliedFrame` helper (broadcast/event-applied-\nframe.ts) hydrates the sidecar at egress for both the live-broadcast path\n(broadcast/event-applied.ts) and the catch-up slice-replay path (handlers/catch-\nup.ts:604–621). The client store (shell/ws/defaultStore.ts) carries the sidecar\nin a per-session `borrowedNodeContent` side map; projectNodes (GraphCanvasPane.tsx)\ngains an `entity-included{node}` arm that emits a StatementNode when the id is\npresent in the map. Test infra fix: two narrow SQL-mock pools taught to recognize\nthe new `SELECT … FROM nodes WHERE id = ANY($1)` queries from loadBorrowedEntities\n(returning empty rows rather than throwing).\n\nCoverage: 18 new Vitest assertions across ws-envelope, frame-helper, shell-store,\nand moderator-projector packages; 1 new Cucumber scenario pinning the slice-path\nwire behavior; Playwright solo-prep-flow.spec.ts extended to open the destination\noperate console and assert the borrowed node renders on the canvas (repays the\ndeferred criterion-6 assertion from xsession_inclusion_render_loader).\n\nRefinement: tasks/refinements/moderator-ui/xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render.md\n\n- packages/shared-types/src/ws-envelope.ts (+.test.ts): optional borrowedNode sidecar on event-applied payload\n- apps/server/src/ws/broadcast/event-applied-frame.ts (+.test.ts): shared buildEventAppliedFrame hydration helper\n- apps/server/src/ws/broadcast/event-applied.ts: live-broadcast egress hydration\n- apps/server/src/ws/broadcast/bus.ts: wired buildEventAppliedFrame\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/catch-up.ts: slice-replay egress hydration\n- apps/server/src/sessions/routes.ts (+.test.ts): loadBorrowedEntities post-commit step; test-infra borrowed-entity SELECT recognition\n- apps/server/src/test-support/concurrent-write-pool.ts: test-infra borrowed-entity SELECT recognition\n- packages/shell/src/ws/store-contract.ts: borrowedNodeContent map on store contract\n- packages/shell/src/ws/defaultStore.ts (+.test.ts): per-session map carry in applyEvent\n- packages/shell/src/ws/client.ts: threaded borrowedNodeContent through WS client\n- apps/moderator/src/graph/GraphCanvasPane.tsx (+.test.tsx): projectNodes borrowed arg + entity-included{node} arm\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/CaptureTargetChip.test.tsx: fixture field add for new slice field\n- apps/participant/src/proposals/useNewProposalArrival.test.ts: fixture field add for new slice field\n- tests/behavior/backend/ws-catch-up.feature (+steps): Cucumber — destination catch-up slice hydrates borrowed node content\n- tests/e2e/solo-prep-flow.spec.ts: Playwright — assert cited node renders on destination canvas\n- tasks/30-moderator-ui.tji: complete 100\n- tasks/refinements/moderator-ui/xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render.md: Status block\n- tasks/parking-lot.md: D3 snapshot-fallback design question parked for human review\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see orchestrator/logs/iter-0009-verify-*.log):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b0683cec16a182860814da9a34cbbc68cf241b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/b0683cec16a182860814da9a34cbbc68cf241b3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDZlMzY4MmFkOWQzMjEwYjNjZmQ2YzE1OGUxMzNhMGNhOGJiYzZiMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356","sha":"b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356"}],"sha":"6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/6e3682ad9d3210b3cfd6c158e133a0ca8bbc6b2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T05:48:12Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T05:48:12Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"backend.cross_session_permissions.xsession_native_edge_annotation_materialization: materialize edges/session_edges and annotations/session_annotations for natively-created entities\n\nExtends materializeEntityRow to cover the four event shapes that were\ndeferred when the node seam shipped in sp_e2e: edge-created->edges,\nannotation-created->annotations, entity-included{edge}->session_edges,\nand entity-included{annotation}->session_annotations. Each INSERT is\nFK-ordered (endpoint entities precede edges; edges precede annotations;\n*-created before entity-included) and ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING for\nidempotency. The commit WS handler is now wired to call materializeEntityRow\nin its append loop -- mandatory because annotation-created and\nADR-0046 interpretive-split edge-created are emitted only at commit time.\nThe methodology commit handler gains a paired entity-included{annotation}\nemit after annotation-created so the session_annotations row lands.\n\nTogether this makes natively-authored edges and annotations visible to\ncanReferenceEdge / canReferenceAnnotation, unblocking cross-session\ncitation of those entity kinds via POST /sessions/:id/include.\n\nRefinement: tasks/refinements/backend/xsession_native_edge_annotation_materialization.md\n\n- apps/server/src/events/materialize.ts: extended for edge-created, annotation-created, entity-included{edge/annotation}; fixed stale ADR ref\n- apps/server/src/events/materialize.test.ts: new Vitest unit coverage (9 cases, all four kinds + polymorphic XOR + no-op)\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/commit.ts: wired materializeEntityRow into commit append loop\n- apps/server/src/methodology/handlers/commit.ts: emit entity-included{annotation} after annotation-created for annotate/meta-move\n- apps/server/src/methodology/handlers/commit.test.ts: updated event-count/order assertions for new emit\n- apps/server/src/methodology/handlers/structural-target.test.ts: updated event-count/order assertions for new emit\n- packages/shell/src/facet-status/facet-status.ts: minor fixup included in this changeset\n- tests/behavior/steps/methodology-commit-meta-move.steps.ts: updated step assertions for new emit\n- tests/behavior/backend/native-edge-annotation-materialization.feature: new Cucumber feature (3 scenarios: edge cite, annotation cite, replay idempotency)\n- tests/behavior/steps/backend-native-edge-annotation-materialization.steps.ts: new Cucumber step definitions (pglite, real migrated schema)\n- tasks/20-backend.tji: complete 100\n- tasks/refinements/backend/xsession_native_edge_annotation_materialization.md: Status block\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain -- see orchestrator/logs/iter-0007-verify-*.log):\n  - pnpm run check -- green.\n  - pnpm run test:smoke -- green.\n  - pnpm run test:behavior:smoke -- green.\n  - make test:e2e:compose -- green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c273d7fd94b31afda44bfe6ab1856baf3f4ab814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/c273d7fd94b31afda44bfe6ab1856baf3f4ab814"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKGIyYTVmYzY3ZWI0OGI5ZGIzNDYzZTQxOTZkNTM5NGVhNTI0MzIzNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7","sha":"ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7"}],"sha":"b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/b2a5fc67eb48b9db3463e4196d5394ea52432356"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T03:43:58Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T03:43:58Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"backend.cross_session_permissions.xsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader: ship server-side borrowed-entity loader for cross-session cited-edge/annotation projection\n\nExtends the predecessor''s borrowed-node loader (xsession_inclusion_render_loader) to resolve\ncross-session cited edges and annotations plus their full transitive FK closure, seeding\ndependencies-first (post-order DFS) so destination projections render instead of throwing\nReplayError.  All 11 full-log projection sites pick up the generalized loader with rename-only\ncall-site changes; the node-only behavior is byte-identical.\n\nRefinement: tasks/refinements/backend/xsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader.md\n\n- apps/server/src/events/borrowed-entities.ts — new generalized loader (replaces borrowed-nodes.ts): batched SELECT per kind, transitive-closure fixpoint walk, throws on unresolvable transitive deps (D4)\n- apps/server/src/events/borrowed-entities.test.ts — Vitest: borrowed-edge closure, annotation→edge closure, omit/empty cases\n- apps/server/src/projection/replay.ts — BorrowedEntities/BorrowedEdge/BorrowedAnnotation types, collectBorrowedEntityIds, recursive guarded post-order seedBorrowedEntityForEvent\n- apps/server/src/projection/replay.test.ts — Vitest: collectBorrowedEntityIds per-kind, edge w/ 2 borrowed endpoint nodes, annotation w/ borrowed target edge, polymorphic annotation endpoint, unresolvable-transitive-dep throws\n- apps/server/src/projection/at-position.ts — threaded generalized BorrowedEntityLoader\n- apps/server/src/projection/at-position.test.ts — Vitest: borrowed-edge closure seeded only at citation position\n- apps/server/src/projection/cache.ts — BorrowedEntityLoader rename\n- apps/server/src/replay/routes.ts — rename-only call-site update\n- apps/server/src/ws/broadcast/proposal-status.ts — rename-only call-site update\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/{catch-up,commit,meta-disagreement,propose,snapshot,vote,withdraw-agreement,withdraw}.ts — rename-only call-site updates\n- tests/behavior/backend/get-session-state.feature — two new Cucumber scenarios: borrowed edge renders with both endpoint nodes; borrowed annotation renders with its target\n- tests/behavior/steps/backend-get-session-state.steps.ts — step implementations for the new scenarios\n- tasks/20-backend.tji — complete 100 on xsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader\n- tasks/30-moderator-ui.tji — register follow-up task xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render_edge_annotation (~1.5d)\n- tasks/99-milestones.tji — wire new task to m_solo_prep (M13)\n- tasks/refinements/backend/xsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader.md — ## Status block appended\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see orchestrator/logs/iter-0005-verify-*.log):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a92fcfde9a4f25b71327d1230d84ff0d457e6c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/a92fcfde9a4f25b71327d1230d84ff0d457e6c48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKGViYzUwNWZjYjRjNWZmMTgxZGIxNjMxMDlhZjQ0Nzg0MDgyMjUyZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d","sha":"60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d"}],"sha":"ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/ebc505fcb4c5ff181db163109af44784082252d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T02:12:26Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T02:12:26Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"backend.cross_session_permissions.xsession_inclusion_render_loader: ship server-side borrowed-node loader for cross-session cited-node projection\n\nCloses the read-side gap where any server-side full-log projection of a\ndestination session that cited a foreign node threw a ReplayError — blocking\nthe operate-console catch-up snapshot, the replay routes, and every\nwrite-handler that rebuilds prior state before a new proposal.\n\nThe loader seeds a borrowed node directly into projection storage just-in-time\nbefore its entity-included event (Decision D1 — no synthetic sequence numbers;\nlastAppliedSequence stays truthful for the catch-up cursor). Resolution comes\nfrom a single batched SELECT from the global nodes table (Decision D2 — the\ncanonical source written by materializeEntityRow on node-created). No\nsource-visibility re-check at render time (Decision D3 — inclusion is a durable\ngrant). All 11 full-log projection sites wired (Decision D4 — no write-time\nlandmine). Scope limited to node inclusions (Decision D5 — edge/annotation\nresolution deferred to xsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader).\n\nRefinement: tasks/refinements/backend/xsession_inclusion_render_loader.md\n\n- apps/server/src/events/borrowed-nodes.ts — new: loadBorrowedNodes(executor, events); batched SELECT by id; loud on unresolvable id\n- apps/server/src/events/borrowed-nodes.test.ts — new: pglite-backed tests (resolves, no-op when empty, omits unresolvable)\n- apps/server/src/projection/replay.ts — BorrowedNode, collectBorrowedNodeIds, seedBorrowedNodeForEvent; projectFromLog optional borrowed map\n- apps/server/src/projection/replay.test.ts — collectBorrowedNodeIds (native/borrowed/mixed) + projectFromLog borrowed-seed cases\n- apps/server/src/projection/at-position.ts — projectAtPosition optional borrowed map; seeds only at citation point\n- apps/server/src/projection/at-position.test.ts — position-fidelity: borrowed node seeded only at its citation, not before\n- apps/server/src/projection/cache.ts — optional borrowedLoader argument threaded through\n- apps/server/src/replay/routes.ts — both replay routes resolve borrowed nodes before projecting\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/catch-up.ts — catch-up snapshot resolves borrowed nodes\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/propose.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/vote.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/commit.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/meta-disagreement.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/withdraw.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/withdraw-agreement.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/snapshot.ts — write-path wired\n- apps/server/src/ws/broadcast/proposal-status.ts — broadcast path wired\n- tests/behavior/backend/get-session-state.feature — Cucumber: destination session citing foreign node renders borrowed node at GET /sessions/:id/state\n- tests/behavior/steps/backend-get-session-state.steps.ts — Cucumber step definitions\n- tasks/refinements/backend/xsession_inclusion_render_loader.md — Status block appended\n- tasks/20-backend.tji — complete 100; registered xsession_inclusion_edge_annotation_render_loader (1d)\n- tasks/30-moderator-ui.tji — registered xsession_inclusion_destination_canvas_render (1.5d) under mod_graph_rendering\n- tasks/99-milestones.tji — M13 depends extended to include both new follow-up tasks\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see orchestrator/logs/iter-0003-verify-*.log):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae63539f436cea1a23328135558229f670cca4d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/ae63539f436cea1a23328135558229f670cca4d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDYwMzc0YjkyYTI0ZmVkMDg2NmQzNzU4Y2ExYzBjNDcyZGU1YjdiOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597","sha":"76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597"}],"sha":"60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/60374b92a24fed0866d3758ca1c0c472de5b7b9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-16T00:54:36Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-16T00:54:36Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_e2e: capstone Playwright e2e for the solo prep flow\n\nLands the terminal e2e spec for the solo-prep group\n(tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_e2e.md): a single Playwright journey\nthat creates a session via the ''Just me — solo prep'' toggle, drives a\nfull capture→classify→decompose graph through real server propose\nround-trips, auto-commits with zero votes, operator axiom-marks as\nself-target, confirms there is no promotion-to-live path, flips the\nsession public, cites a node into a new session, and asserts it arrives\nstance-free; per-locale (en-US, pt-BR, es-419) axe scans on the operate\nconsole. Discharges the deferred-e2e debt named by all five predecessors\n(sp_session_solo_flag, sp_agreement_satisfied, sp_operator_position_acts,\nsp_create_toggle, sp_mod_solo_ui).\n\nThe spec surfaced a pre-existing write-path gap: propose had never\nmaterialized the global `nodes` + `session_nodes` join rows that\n`canReferenceNode` reads for cross-session citations — so natively-created\nnodes could never be cited (403 entity-not-referenceable). Fixed by\n`apps/server/src/events/materialize.ts` (`materializeEntityRow`) called\ninside the same transaction after each event append. Edge/annotation\nmaterialization and destination-side rendering of cited nodes are left as\nregistered follow-up tasks wired to m_solo_prep.\n\nThe axe scan surfaced a nested-interactive violation: React Flow''s default\n`nodesFocusable` stamps `role=\"button\"` on every node wrapper, conflicting\nwith our inner focusable cards. Fixed by `nodesFocusable={false}` on\n`<ReactFlow>` in `GraphCanvasPane.tsx`; inner keyboard reachability is\npreserved via the card''s own `tabIndex={0}` and native `<button>` elements.\n\nFiles:\n- tests/e2e/solo-prep-flow.spec.ts — new capstone spec (per-locale UI\n  journey + locale-agnostic API steps for make-public + cite)\n- playwright.config.ts — chromium-solo-prep-{en-US,pt-BR,es-419} projects\n- apps/server/src/events/materialize.ts — new event→relational write-path\n  helper (nodes + session_nodes on node-created/entity-included)\n- apps/server/src/ws/handlers/propose.ts — calls materializeEntityRow in\n  the propose append loop (same transaction)\n- apps/moderator/src/graph/GraphCanvasPane.tsx — nodesFocusable={false}\n  to fix axe nested-interactive violations\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — solo_prep.sp_e2e: complete 100\n- tasks/20-backend.tji — registered xsession_inclusion_render_loader and\n  xsession_native_edge_annotation_materialization under\n  backend.cross_session_permissions, wired to m_solo_prep\n- tasks/99-milestones.tji — m_solo_prep: depends extended with both new\n  debt tasks\n- tasks/parking-lot.md — two moderator-UI gap entries from D2 (privacy\n  toggle, citation UI)\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_e2e.md — Status: Done 2026-06-15\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain):\n  - check: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0001-verify-check.log)\n  - vitest: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0001-verify-vitest.log)\n  - cucumber: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0001-verify-cucumber.log)\n  - playwright: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0001-verify-playwright.log)\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"87b812ec600d2edc623a7b4857fc68c53a78f8ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/87b812ec600d2edc623a7b4857fc68c53a78f8ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDc2ZDgxNjdhNGNhMzVhM2E4YjdkNGRhMDNmMzc0OTM3MDU5OWE1OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a","sha":"104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a"}],"sha":"76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/76d8167a4ca35a3a8b7d4da03f3749370599a597"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T20:23:12Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T20:23:12Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_mod_solo_ui: client facet-status solo branch + axiom-mark self-target\n\nTeaches the client facet-status mirror the same Rule 7 solo corollary the\nserver already has (empty non-moderator set + candidate + solo → ''agreed''),\nso commit/substance affordances mount on a solo /m console without a second\nparticipant. Offers the lone operator as the axiom-mark self-target in solo\nmode (gated strictly on session.solo — non-solo path unchanged). A thin\nPlaywright spec covers the pre-satisfied commit affordance, the axiom-mark\nself-target, and an axe WCAG 2.0/2.1 A/AA scan against the compose stack.\nA fixer widened five replay-routes.test.ts beforeEach migration-hook\ntimeouts from 10 s to 30 s to absorb contention under parallel smoke load.\nCloses the client surfacing deferred by sp_agreement_satisfied and\nsp_operator_position_acts; gates sp_e2e. Refinement:\ntasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_mod_solo_ui.md.\n\n- packages/shell/src/facet-status/facet-status.ts — solo branch in derive()\n- packages/shell/src/facet-status/facet-status.test.ts — mirror parity pins sp1–sp5\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/AxiomMarkSubmenu.tsx — deriveSessionSolo/deriveModerator + solo self-target\n- apps/moderator/src/layout/AxiomMarkSubmenu.test.tsx — solo self-target unit tests\n- tests/e2e/solo-moderator-console.spec.ts — new thin Playwright spec\n- apps/server/src/replay/routes.test.ts — fixer: 30s migration-hook timeout\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — complete 100 for sp_mod_solo_ui\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_mod_solo_ui.md — Status block appended\n- tasks/parking-lot.md — solo audience/replay labeling question parked\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see orchestrator/logs/iter-0013-*):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d7312d3a1c863438be42f2b15e97689c069a03a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/d7312d3a1c863438be42f2b15e97689c069a03a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDEwNGY1NDhhYmUxYTYxZTVhZDkxMWE2Mzc1YWNlOWM1NjIxMjUzOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa","sha":"15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa"}],"sha":"104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/104f548abe1a61e5ad911a6375ace9c56212539a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T19:15:29Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T19:15:29Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_discovery_badge: add Solo prep badge to My Sessions rows\n\nBadges solo-session rows in the My Sessions discovery list so a one-person\nworldview-mapping session is visually distinct from a two-sided live debate.\nThe badge is rendered via a new SoloSessionBadge component injected through\nthe existing renderRowActions slot, carrying the solo flag out-of-band through\na fetcher id→solo map and a soloById route ref — zero shared-component changes,\nexactly mirroring the established role-badge mechanism (sd_my_sessions_page D5).\nSee tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_discovery_badge.md.\n\n- apps/root/src/discovery/SoloSessionBadge.tsx — new component; localized pill with data-testid, aria-label; null for non-solo\n- apps/root/src/discovery/SoloSessionBadge.test.tsx — new; asserts label/aria/data-* for true and null for false/undefined\n- apps/root/src/discovery/mySessionsFetcher.ts — MySessionResponseRow gains solo; MySessionsPage gains id→solo map\n- apps/root/src/discovery/mySessionsFetcher.test.ts — extended with solo correlation fixture\n- apps/root/src/routes/MySessionsRoute.tsx — soloById ref + SoloSessionBadge in renderRowActions\n- apps/root/src/routes/MySessionsRoute.test.tsx — extended: badge present on solo row, absent on non-solo\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/en-US.json — discovery.mySessions.solo.{label,ariaLabel}\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/pt-BR.json — same keys, parity maintained\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/es-419.json — same keys, parity maintained (930 keys all 3 locales)\n- tests/e2e/my-sessions-page.spec.ts — createSession gains optional solo; presence/absence + WCAG_AA axe scenario\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — sp_discovery_badge marked complete 100\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_discovery_badge.md — Status block appended\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see orchestrator/logs/iter-0011-verify-*.log):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"59ab53b84f9f045cddc2f72218922ac11b577cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/59ab53b84f9f045cddc2f72218922ac11b577cc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDE1ZDU3YmNjNGU5MDUxZmM4YmU1YzAwNjgyNTMyZTE0ZDBiNDVjZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361","sha":"76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361"}],"sha":"15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/15d57bcc4e9051fc8be5c00682532e14d0b45cfa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:38:17Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T18:38:17Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_create_toggle: add \"Just me — solo prep\" checkbox to New Session form\n\nAdds a native checkbox to the existing moderator New Session form\n(apps/moderator/src/routes/CreateSession.tsx) that sets solo: true on\nthe POST /api/sessions request the form already sends. The backend\nalready accepted the optional solo field (sp_session_solo_flag); this\nleaf makes it reachable from the UI.\n\nThe solo field is always included in the request body as a boolean\n(mirroring how privacy is always sent), so the payload is deterministic\nand the component tests can assert an exact object. Defaults to off —\na session is a live debate unless the user ticks the box.\n\nLocalized across all three catalogs (moderator.createSession.solo.{label,\ndescription} in en-US/pt-BR/es-419) per ADR 0024; keys registered in\nthe CREATE_SESSION_KEYS parity list with canonical en-US pins. Axe\nWCAG AA scan of /m/sessions/new added in create-session-flow.spec.ts\nper ADR 0040, paying down previously-missing coverage on that route.\n\n- apps/moderator/src/routes/CreateSession.tsx — solo state, checkbox after privacy fieldset, solo in POST body, header comment\n- apps/moderator/src/routes/CreateSession.test.tsx — solo default-off, solo-on payload, render structure\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/en-US.json — solo.{label,description}\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/pt-BR.json — solo.{label,description}\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/catalogs/es-419.json — solo.{label,description}\n- packages/i18n-catalogs/src/moderator-create-session.test.ts — two new keys + canonical en-US pins\n- tests/e2e/create-session-flow.spec.ts — solo toggle present/operable, solo creation lands on invite, axe no violations\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — complete 100 for sp_create_toggle\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_create_toggle.md — Status block\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see orchestrator/logs/iter-0009-verify-*.log):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c7f20528c6f6a0699324f1947d7bc422d9df0e7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/c7f20528c6f6a0699324f1947d7bc422d9df0e7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDc2OTQ4MDg1ZmRjMzczYWNkM2UwZWNkODg0ODZkMjA0ZTk2NmMzNjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960","sha":"488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960"}],"sha":"76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/76948085fdc373acd3e0ecd88486d204e966c361"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:59:27Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:59:27Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_operator_position_acts: enforce solo-gated moderator axiom-mark + pin position acts\n\nImplements ADR 0049 decision (2): the lone operator in a solo session may\naxiom-mark and hold substance stances.  The critical deliverable is making\nthe neutral-moderator invariant *enforced and tested* rather than merely\nemergent — before this change a moderator could propose a self-axiom-mark\nin a real debate that would dangle awaiting debater ratification; now that\npath is an explicit engine rejection (`moderator-cannot-hold-position`).\n\nSubstance is deliberately left ungated: moderators legitimately propose\nsubstance candidates in real debates as part of board-driving, and what\nturns those candidates into a debater''s position is the agreement walk\n(already solo-aware via sp_agreement_satisfied), not the propose step.\n\nEngine changes (propose side only; replay/projection/commit unchanged):\n- `apps/server/src/methodology/handlers/propose.ts` — import\n  `requesterIsModerator`; add solo-gated Rule 4 to\n  `validateAxiomMarkProposal`; renumber duplicate rule to 5.\n- `apps/server/src/methodology/types.ts` — add `RejectionReason`\n  `''moderator-cannot-hold-position''` (D2 honest kebab; distinct from\n  `axiom-mark-not-self` which is about identity, not role).\n- `apps/server/src/errors.ts` — map new reason → 403 (grouped with\n  `axiom-mark-not-self`).\n\nTest additions:\n- `apps/server/src/methodology/handlers/proposeAxiomMark.test.ts` —\n  `seedSoloSession` helper + Rule 4 block: non-solo moderator rejected,\n  solo moderator accepted, debater accepted regardless of solo (3 new\n  Vitest cases; 12 total pass).\n- `tests/behavior/methodology/solo-operator-position-acts.feature` —\n  3 Cucumber scenarios: solo axiom-mark self (projection keyed by\n  moderator id), solo set-node-substance (facet derives agreed/committed),\n  guard non-solo moderator rejected + debater accepted.\n- `tests/behavior/steps/methodology-solo-operator-position.steps.ts` —\n  step definitions for the new feature.\n\nExhaustive-surface follow-ups (fixer pass):\n- `apps/server/src/errors.test.ts`, `apps/server/src/ws/protocol-docs.test.ts`\n  — added new reason to both `Record<RejectionReason, true>` maps and the\n  runtime equality array (TS2741/TS2322/TS1360 fixes).\n- `docs/ws-protocol.md` — documented wire code for new reason.\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain — see\n- check: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0007-verify-check.log)\n- vitest: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0007-verify-vitest.log)\n- cucumber: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0007-verify-cucumber.log)\n- playwright: PASS (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0007-verify-playwright.log)):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba325bf175424b50a21170f6b8718e9209617a18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/ba325bf175424b50a21170f6b8718e9209617a18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDQ4ODA1MmE1ODUyN2RjZWY2NjRmYjQxMDY1NTM5Yzk1ZDk3MzE5NjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4","sha":"fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4"}],"sha":"488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/488052a58527dcef664fb41065539c95d9731960"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:06:21Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T17:06:21Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_agreement_satisfied: engine + projection treat solo party-of-one as agreement-satisfied\n\nImplements ADR 0049 Decision §1: for a solo session the unanimity predicate is\nvacuously satisfied the moment the sole host/moderator acts — the commit gate\npasses and the facet derives ''agreed'', so the lone moderator''s facet-keyed and\nstructural commits land without any debater vote. The non-solo path is unchanged:\na live session with zero debaters still rejects with unanimous-agree-required.\n\nThree seams changed, all gated on projection.solo:\n- commit.ts: both checkUnanimousAgreeFacet and checkUnanimousAgreeStructural\n  return null (satisfied) for solo empty non-moderator set; non-solo still rejects.\n- facet-status.ts: deriveFacetStatusFromState rule 7 derives ''agreed'' for solo\n  empty-set with a candidate; rule 2 (no candidate → awaiting-proposal) still wins.\n- projection.ts + replay.ts: Projection gains #solo / get solo / setSolo;\n  handleSessionCreated reads payload.solo and calls setSolo — the flag is available\n  identically on the live wire and under replay.\n\nTest surface:\n- apps/server/src/methodology/handlers/commit.test.ts — solo facet-keyed accept,\n  non-solo facet-keyed reject, solo structural accept, non-solo structural reject\n- apps/server/src/projection/facet-status.test.ts — solo+candidate→agreed,\n  solo+no-candidate→awaiting-proposal, non-solo+candidate→proposed\n- apps/server/src/projection/replay.test.ts — handleSessionCreated captures solo\n- tests/behavior/methodology/commit-solo-agreement.feature — Cucumber: solo\n  facet-keyed auto-commit, solo structural auto-commit, non-solo zero-debater\n  rejection (safety pin)\n- tests/behavior/steps/methodology-commit-solo.steps.ts — step definitions\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain):\n  - pnpm run check — green.\n  - pnpm run test:smoke — green.\n  - pnpm run test:behavior:smoke — green.\n  - make test:e2e:compose — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7df197251a35eae6a34a005b3f4ff5d71d779c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/b7df197251a35eae6a34a005b3f4ff5d71d779c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKGZjODg5NTMxNTgzMGE4ZDljZTU1ZTcwYjYxNGRjMjg5ZTdlYjA5ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5","sha":"d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5"}],"sha":"fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/fc8895315830a8d9ce55e70b614dc289e7eb09f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T16:20:36Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T16:20:36Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_session_solo_flag: add solo boolean to sessions + thread through creation path\n\nImplements the backend foundation for M13 Solo Prep: a `solo BOOLEAN NOT NULL\nDEFAULT false` column on the sessions table, threaded end-to-end through\nsession creation so the flag is persisted on the row, recorded in the\n`session-created` event payload, and exposed on SessionResponse and\nMySessionResponse. Mirrors the privacy seam wholesale per ADR 0049.\n\nThe boolean shape was chosen over a TEXT+CHECK enum: there is exactly one\naxis today (solo vs. not), every downstream branch is a plain truth-test,\nand `solo` is a departure flag (like `archived`) rather than two symmetric\nfirst-class values like `privacy`. The flag is immutable after creation; no\ntoggle endpoint is added.\n\n- apps/server/migrations/0020_sessions_solo.sql — ADD COLUMN solo BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false\n- packages/shared-types/src/events.ts — sessionCreatedPayloadSchema gains required solo: z.boolean()\n- apps/server/src/sessions/routes.ts — createSessionBodySchema (optional solo), handler default, INSERT/RETURNING, event payload, types, mappers, response schemas\n- apps/server/src/sessions/routes.test.ts — atomic solo=true row+event assert; defaulted-false case; non-boolean → 400\n- packages/shared-types/src/events.test.ts — validateEvent rejects session-created missing solo / non-boolean solo\n- packages/shared-types/src/limits.test.ts — base fixture patched with solo: false (fixer''s fix)\n- tests/behavior/backend/create-session.feature — solo=true round-trip + default-false Cucumber scenarios\n- tests/behavior/steps/backend-create-session.steps.ts — step implementations for both scenarios\n- ~95 test/fixture sites across diagnostics, methodology handlers, projection, ws-handlers, test-mode, walkthrough data — solo: false threaded so validateEvent stays green\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — complete 100\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_session_solo_flag.md — Status block appended\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0003-verify-check.log).\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0003-verify-vitest.log).\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0003-verify-cucumber.log).\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green (log: orchestrator/logs/iter-0003-verify-playwright.log); 2 environmental flakes (net::ERR_NETWORK_CHANGED on login nav; 1200ms flash-clear timeout under load) unrelated to the solo change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e3969caaa7b759faecbfbc39aa19148a5ef19432","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/e3969caaa7b759faecbfbc39aa19148a5ef19432"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKGQ1MDYzNGJiZDE4NjM3ODE3Yzk3MDdiNjU1ODc5ZmRiMTQyYWMwZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c","sha":"2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c"}],"sha":"d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/d50634bbd18637817c9707b655879fdb142ac0f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T14:28:51Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T14:28:51Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo_prep.sp_adr: record ADR 0049 — solo-prep invariant bends\n\nRecords the two foundational semantic decisions for the Solo Prep\nmilestone (M13) in a dedicated ADR, as called for by docs/solo-prep.md\nTracking (lines 128–139). Both decisions were settled in the design\ndoc; this ADR lifts them into the canonical ADR convention so every\nsuccessor leaf (sp_session_solo_flag, sp_agreement_satisfied,\nsp_operator_position_acts, and the rest) builds on a single\nauthoritative record rather than re-deriving the semantics.\n\nDecision 1 — Agreement satisfied-by-construction: the per-facet /\nper-participant agreement rule is evaluated for a party of one; with\none participant the set is trivially satisfied, so the session\nauto-commits. Framed as evaluation, not bypass, so the live-debate\npath is unchanged and the commit projector stays single.\n\nDecision 2 — Operator holds the position: the lone host/moderator\nperforms both operator acts and the acts normally reserved to a debater\n(axiom-mark, substance stances), gated on a `solo` flag so the\nneutral-moderator rule still binds real debates.\n\nRejected alternatives documented: bypass-the-machinery (forks the\ncommit flow), hidden-second-seat / both-sides (larger out-of-scope\nmode), dedicated solo session type (code-sharing cost, no gain).\n\nColumn shape (boolean vs. mode-enum) intentionally deferred to\nsp_session_solo_flag. No predecessor-ADR amendment sweep — ADR 0030\nis cited as reused, not amended.\n\n- docs/adr/0049-solo-prep-party-of-one-agreement-and-operator-position.md — new ADR, 163 lines\n- tasks/78-solo-prep.tji — sp_adr marked complete 100\n- tasks/refinements/solo_prep/sp_adr.md — Status block appended\n\nVerification (driver-run, deterministic chain):\n  - `pnpm run check` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:smoke` — green.\n  - `pnpm run test:behavior:smoke` — green.\n  - `make test:e2e:compose` — green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e6802e7ae28d47b20217667ac7bbe4652542a69c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/e6802e7ae28d47b20217667ac7bbe4652542a69c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c","node_id":"C_kwDOSZCY7doAKDJhMWU3ZTMxZmViNTU2YTQzMWNkNmVkNzhlOWE4NDhjZjYxZWFjMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso/a-conversa/commit/0e148e82c6ffa8012eb77dbd5ce1caca2cbcfdaa","sha":"0e148e82c6ffa8012eb77dbd5ce1caca2cbcfdaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/0e148e82c6ffa8012eb77dbd5ce1caca2cbcfdaa"}],"sha":"2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/2a1e7e31feb556a431cd6ed78e9a848cf61eac0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/commits/0e148e82c6ffa8012eb77dbd5ce1caca2cbcfdaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-14T13:49:55Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-14T13:49:55Z","email":"daniel@ruoso.com","name":"Daniel Ruoso"},"message":"solo-prep: add design doc + WBS group (M13)\n\nPlan Solo Prep — a single-participant session where one person maps\ntheir own side of a topic alone. New docs/solo-prep.md (linked from\nDESIGN.md), the solo_prep WBS group (tasks/78-solo-prep.tji, brief\nscopes only — refinement/implementation come later), and milestone\nm_solo_prep (M13).\n\nDesign: a `solo` flag reuses the whole session machinery; with no\ndebater seat the lone host/moderator is also the sole position-holder,\nso the agreement rule is satisfied-by-construction (auto-commit) and the\noperator gains the debater-only acts (axiom-mark, substance). Public\nprep nodes stay citable; promotion into a live debate is out of scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8b9203c45a3b52a1db7e86220418270519e1b7df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/trees/8b9203c45a3b52a1db7e86220418270519e1b7df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ruoso/a-conversa/git/commits/0e148e82c6ffa8012eb77dbd5ce1caca2cbcfdaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81195?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ruoso","id":81195,"login":"ruoso","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTk1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ruoso/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/