te":"2026-10-04T15:24:07Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"coder fix","tree":{"sha":"4bbfc97695733ef8282c0c7315dcc7177f13b496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/4bbfc97695733ef8282c0c7315dcc7177f13b496"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/fd9ce6142cd03a10d2d1a0208df90020e59deed2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/fd9ce6142cd03a10d2d1a0208df90020e59deed2","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKGZkOWNlNjE0MmNkMDNhMTBkMmQxYTAyMDhkZjkwMDIwZTU5ZGVlZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f","sha":"40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f"}],"sha":"fd9ce6142cd03a10d2d1a0208df90020e59deed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/fd9ce6142cd03a10d2d1a0208df90020e59deed2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:37:30Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:37:30Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"fix(develop): cloud dev environments that are actually ready\n\nA cloud development environment built, reported `running`, and then no IDE\ncould ever attach to it. The agent inside the pod was being refused:\n\n  401: User is not active (status = \"dormant\"). Contact an admin to\n  reactivate your account.\n\nCoder marks an account dormant after a stretch of inactivity. It will still\naccept a workspace *create* for that user — 201, build succeeds, status\n`running` — but the workspace agent cannot authenticate, so it retries until\nit times out. Everything upstream looks healthy and the environment is dead.\n\nTwo fixes, because there were two faults.\n\n**The cause.** `/api/coder/identity` already matches the signed-in user to a\nCoder account; it now also clears dormancy on the one it finds. Dormancy is\ncleared by signing in, and the person has just signed in to the console.\n`suspended` is deliberately left alone — that is an administrator disabling an\naccount, and a console page should not quietly undo it; it is reported\ninstead.\n\n**The lie.** The page read `latest_build.status` and called anything `running`\nready: it showed \"1 running\" for a workspace whose agent had timed out, and\noffered VS Code and IntelliJ buttons that could only open a dead app. Build\nstate and usability are different questions. A workspace is now `ready` only\nwhen its agent is connected and past its startup script; the strip counts\nReady rather than Running and says how many are unreachable; IDE and terminal\nactions are gated on that; and a workspace that is running-but-unreachable\nsays why on the card.\n\nVerified end to end against the cluster: an environment created for a dormant\nowner went from agent `timeout` to `connected` / lifecycle `ready` with\n`code-server` healthy, and the page from \"1 running\" to \"READY 1\".\n\n12 tests on the readiness model, including the timed-out agent that started\nthis, a connected agent still running its startup script, and a status this\nconsole has not seen never counting as ready.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"021d1f562dc383b18d8d9b20f54011e882f74c55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/021d1f562dc383b18d8d9b20f54011e882f74c55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKDQwYzZiMTI0Y2Q2ZjQxY2JkMGY0OTMwYTBhYjgzMzI0ZTg4MDUyOGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b","sha":"903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b"}],"sha":"40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/40c6b124cd6f41cbd0f4930a0ab83324e880528f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:49:22Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:49:22Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"fix(develop): render a README the way a README is meant to look\n\nTwo different renderers were drawing the same file. The Files tab used the\nshared one from `shell-ui`; the repository drawer had its own, which built an\nHTML string and injected it with `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. So the same README\nlooked different depending which surface you opened it from, and the drawer''s\ncopy supported no tables, clamped every image to 24px tall, and was the only\nplace in the console assembling markup by string concatenation.\n\nThe drawer now uses the shared renderer, and the bespoke one is gone.\n\nThe shared renderer rendered every image as its alt text. That is the right\nrule for the assistant — model output must not make this console fetch from\nsomeone else''s CDN, and it has to work air-gapped — but applied to a\nrepository README it meant every badge and every screenshot was a word of grey\ntext. Images are now a per-call policy: the assistant keeps alt text, the\nuser''s own repository content shows the image.\n\nMaking that work needed the sources, which the tokenizer was discarding, and a\nway to resolve them. A README writes `./docs/arch.png`, `../logo.svg`,\n`/screenshots/home.png` — none of which mean anything to a browser pointed at\nthe console. They resolve onto Gitea''s raw endpoint through the console''s own\nauthenticated proxy, so private repositories work and nothing is fetched from\noutside. External URLs pass through untouched, a `..` too many cannot climb\nout of the repository, and anything unresolvable keeps its alt text rather\nthan becoming a broken image icon.\n\nHeadings are real `h1`–`h6` elements now, too. A README is a document with a\nstructure and a screen reader cannot navigate a stack of divs.\n\n20 tests: the tokenizer carrying sources through the linked-badge case that\nstarted all this, image titles not being mistaken for part of the URL, and the\npath resolution including the climb-out attempt.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b85d28d90685475dcd09b03f85d393026e968df6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/b85d28d90685475dcd09b03f85d393026e968df6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKDkwM2M1MTlmYzNmMmIxZTA5ZmJlMGU5NjllMGIxNzMzZThlZGMyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95","sha":"27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95"}],"sha":"903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/903c519fc3f2b1e09fbe0e969e0b1733e8edc22b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:38:37Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:38:37Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"feat(deliver): follow every commit through the pipeline, for custom apps\n\nThe Delivery Flow showed the newest of everything: the newest commit, the\nnewest build, whatever the stages happen to hold. That answers \"how is the\npipeline right now\" and not \"where did my change get to\", which is the\nquestion people open it with.\n\nBelow the stage canvas there is now a commit trail: every commit on the\nbranch, each with its own journey through committed → pull request → build →\nfreight → promotion → deployed, as a row of pips that expands into the detail\nof each step. The commit that is actually running is marked Live.\n\nThe join key is the commit sha, and every tool records it somewhere different:\n\n  - Tekton publishes the resolved commit as a pipeline *result*. The\n    `revision` parameter is the branch — this platform''s release pipelines\n    pass `main` — so a parameter is only believed when it looks like a sha.\n    Reading it blindly would have compared a commit against the word \"main\".\n  - kpack puts it on the build''s source, Kargo inside its freight, Argo CD as\n    the synced revision.\n  - Lengths differ everywhere: Gitea returns a 40-character sha and a\n    10-character short one, a tag may carry seven. Comparison is by common\n    prefix with git''s own seven-character minimum, because `===` missed every\n    one of those pairings and made built commits look unbuilt.\n\nWhere a tool genuinely does not say, the step is `unknown` rather than\nassumed: a build system that is unreachable is not the same as one that never\nbuilt this commit, and a commit pushed straight to the branch never had a pull\nrequest — that is `skipped`, not a gap.\n\nScoped to custom applications, per the request. The platform''s own packages\nare installed from its release channel rather than built from this repository\nper commit, so walking one through \"Code → PR → Build\" would describe\nsomething that never happened; the picker now lists only applications without\nthe platform''s labels, and says so when there are none.\n\n23 tests, most of them on the sha matching and on where each tool hides the\nrevision.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"066f1563485664c5e258ca71f14f4abc5c06360a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/066f1563485664c5e258ca71f14f4abc5c06360a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKDI3ZDUyNTBmZTQ3NzQ5N2QxODdjNjVhZTE0NDQ0MTQ4ODlmY2FhOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/fe554c6834f9c7a4068dc72b67e38f1b39e8afe0","sha":"fe554c6834f9c7a4068dc72b67e38f1b39e8afe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/fe554c6834f9c7a4068dc72b67e38f1b39e8afe0"}],"sha":"27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/27d5250fe477497d187c65ae1444414889fcaa95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/fe554c6834f9c7a4068dc72b67e38f1b39e8afe0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:38:24Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T13:38:24Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"fix(deliver): show every Argo CD application, filtered by what it is\n\nThe page read \"Showing 0 of 75 applications — scoped to platform\". The team\nlens filtered on `spec.project` being an Argo CD project owned by the active\nteam; every Application on this platform is in the `default` Argo project and\nno workspace project claims it, so the lens matched nothing. A filter that\nhides everything is not a lens, it is a blank page — and it hid the whole\nfleet behind a concept that does not apply here.\n\nThe page now shows everything and narrows by what the platform already\nrecords. Every package it installs carries `adhar.io/category` —\n`application`, `data`, `security`, `observability`, `core`, `ai`,\n`infrastructure` — and `adhar.io/package-name`. An Application without those\nlabels was not installed by the platform: it is something a team deployed.\n\nSo the filters are Custom apps / Platform across the top, and the categories\nactually present underneath. Only categories with applications in them are\noffered, since offering a filter that can only produce an empty list is how\nthe page got into this state. Custom/Platform only appears when there is\nsomething on both sides of it.\n\nThe classification is a label check and nothing cleverer. Guessing from the\nrepository URL or the namespace would misfile the first workload that happens\nto live in the platform''s git org.\n\nThe two empty states left are the honest ones — no applications at all, and\nno matches — and the second now offers to clear the filters.\n\n13 tests, including a category this console has never seen being kept rather\nthan dropped, and blank labels not counting as a category.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f342d163737be91580317d3582e23844c68da70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/0f342d163737be91580317d3582e23844c68da70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/fe554c6834f9c7a4068dc72b67e38f1b39e8afe0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"http