":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/d8e6229025ff7f419d052b1009f702e42ac5c807","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKGQ4ZTYyMjkwMjVmZjdmNDE5ZDA1MmIxMDA5ZjcwMmU0MmFjNWM4MDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917","sha":"0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917"}],"sha":"d8e6229025ff7f419d052b1009f702e42ac5c807","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/d8e6229025ff7f419d052b1009f702e42ac5c807"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:45:50Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:45:50Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"feat(develop): a real editor in Repository Files, bundled not fetched\n\nThe Files tab rendered every file as monospace text in a two-column\ntable — line number, line — so a Go service and a .gitignore looked\nidentical and nothing was highlighted, foldable or searchable. Monaco,\nthe editor VS Code is built on, was already wrapped in this module for\nother screens; the viewer just never used it.\n\nIt does now, with grammar-aware highlighting, folding, bracket matching,\na minimap and ⌘F. A path tells Monaco which grammar to use, so there is\na resolver for that: ~90 extensions, plus whole-name matches because\n`go.mod` and `go.sum` share a family but not a grammar and\n`Dockerfile.dev` is still a Dockerfile. Unknown extensions degrade to\nplain text rather than guessing.\n\nThree things the old viewer got wrong by having only one mode: an image\nis now shown as an image instead of decoded into mojibake, a binary is\nrefused before anything tries to read it as text — by extension, and by\na NUL byte for the ones with no extension at all — and a file past\n800 KB falls back to plain text, because Monaco tokenises the whole\nbuffer up front and would freeze the tab.\n\nNO CDN. Monaco was pulled from jsDelivr at runtime, with a `data:`\nworker shim to get its language services past the cross-origin Worker\nrule. None of that can work on an air-gapped install, which is the normal\nshape of this platform: the editor simply never appeared. It is a\ndependency now and Vite bundles it — 3.3 MB of editor and a 231 KB\nworker, emitted as local assets, behind a dynamic import so they are\nfetched from this origin the first time an editor mounts rather than on\nevery page load.\n\nAuditing for that turned up a second one: the design module pulled\nMermaid from jsDelivr the same way, so diagrams never rendered there\neither. Bundled on the same terms. There is now no `jsdelivr`, `unpkg`\nor `cdnjs` reference left in any source file or any build output, and a\npage load makes zero external requests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6693ca048d0901245d4ce091cd8662be1dc0a4c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/6693ca048d0901245d4ce091cd8662be1dc0a4c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKDBiYmNlMzU3MDZhZmM4ZTk2ZDc5NGUzZDViMjQ3YTA2YWVlZGE5MTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/2822e27981d76896a9b396a8b590e10014273aaa","sha":"2822e27981d76896a9b396a8b590e10014273aaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/2822e27981d76896a9b396a8b590e10014273aaa"}],"sha":"0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/0bbce35706afc8e96d794e3d5b247a06aeeda917"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/2822e27981d76896a9b396a8b590e10014273aaa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:34:00Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:34:00Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"feat(develop): repositories read as owner/name, and section by owner\n\nA repository was listed by its bare name. `packages` could belong to\nanyone; `adhar/packages` could not — and the qualifier was already in the\ndata, as Gitea''s `full_name`, just never shown. With a handful of repos\nthat is a small loss of context; with a few hundred under several teams\nit is the only thing that would tell them apart.\n\nThe name is qualified in all three layouts, with the owner set a step\nback from the name so it reads as context rather than as half the title,\nthe way a path does. Search matches the qualified form too, so typing\n\"adhar/pack\" finds it written the way it is displayed.\n\nThe list also sections by owner — but only once a second owner exists.\nOn a one-org install every repo shares an owner and a heading over the\nwhole list is furniture, so there is none; the sections appear exactly\nwhen they start carrying information, which is when another team''s org\nor a fork from elsewhere shows up. Section order follows the list''s own\nsort, because alphabetising here would quietly override whatever the\noperator chose to sort by.\n\nThe grouping lives in `data/repo-grouping.ts` rather than in the view:\nthe Deno test runner has no React in its import map, so logic reachable\nfrom a `.tsx` cannot be unit-tested. Same arrangement, same reason, as\n`nav-ownership.ts` beside `nav-item.tsx`. 7 tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ab4d84ae066dad9e908b5648566db33e78203b8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/ab4d84ae066dad9e908b5648566db33e78203b8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/2822e27981d76896a9b396a8b590e10014273aaa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4jav