events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/5f73672f1a311cd47be7e41cdaed2f914b2cfda8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:49:56Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:49:56Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"feat(ai): a landing you can read at a glance\n\nEight agent cards, each with an avatar, a name, an all-caps role, two lines\nof description, a tool count and an @handle, made a wall of near-identical\nboxes with nothing for the eye to land on — and \"CONSOLE AGENT\" repeated six\ntimes down the page said nothing, because console is the default and only the\nruntime ones are worth marking at all. What a person does on that page is\npick who answers, so an agent is now a picker row: accent, name, the size of\nits toolkit, and \"answering\" on the selected one. The description it dropped\nis still one line below, as the heading of that agent''s prompts, and the\nwhole of it is in the tile''s title.\n\nThe prompts were a two-column grid holding three cards, so the last cell was\na hole the width of a card — and the count varies per agent, so it was a hole\nof a different shape for each. They are one list now, which cannot be ragged.\n\nTogether that is about a third of the height for the same content, and the\nroster reads as a row of choices rather than a page of profiles.","tree":{"sha":"5edd19c7b61b9461a4892aa1ff5883baade7009a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/5edd19c7b61b9461a4892aa1ff5883baade7009a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/5f73672f1a311cd47be7e41cdaed2f914b2cfda8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/5f73672f1a311cd47be7e41cdaed2f914b2cfda8","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKDVmNzM2NzJmMWEzMTFjZDQ3YmU3ZTQxY2RhZWQyZjkxNGIyY2ZkYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94","sha":"8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94"}],"sha":"5f73672f1a311cd47be7e41cdaed2f914b2cfda8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/5f73672f1a311cd47be7e41cdaed2f914b2cfda8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:46:22Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:46:22Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"feat(develop): Cloud Envs opens VS Code, IntelliJ and a terminal that work\n\nThe Repositories page learned to mint a Coder session before opening an IDE;\nthe Cloud Envs page never did. Every \"Open IDE\", every app chip and every\n\"Terminal\" there built a plain Coder URL and handed it to a new tab — which\narrives on Coder''s domain with no session, so it landed on a sign-in page, or\non a 404 for a workspace the visitor was not allowed to see. Those are the\nsame links, on the page whose whole job is opening environments.\n\nAll of them now go through the BFF, which resolves whose workspace it is,\nmints a short-lived token for that owner and returns a URL carrying it. One\nhelper does it for apps and terminals alike, and reports a blocked pop-up\nrather than leaving a click that did nothing.\n\nThe endpoint grew a `kind: ''terminal''` mode, because a workspace''s terminal is\nserved by the same app proxy on the same domain and needs the same session —\nit just names no app.\n\nIntelliJ is offered here at all now. The page only ever looked for a\ncode-server app, so the JetBrains Gateway link the template ships was\ninvisible: the one place listing your environments could not open the IDE\nhalf of them are used with. Its deep link carries the same token, so Gateway\nno longer asks for one to be pasted in. The browser-IDE matcher also stopped\nmatching `vscode-desktop`, which had made \"Open IDE\" hand a `vscode://` URL\nto a browser tab.\n\nVerified against the live cluster: a workspace was created from the\nRepositories page, and code-server, the JetBrains deep link, the VS Code\nDesktop deep link and the terminal all come back with a token; the two\nbrowser URLs answer 200.","tree":{"sha":"5945c4f2da7503418cf6ca6d74a889d14999e534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/5945c4f2da7503418cf6ca6d74a889d14999e534"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94","node_id":"C_kwDOSZcuM9oAKDhlMWNkMTRmMzkwNzE5OWZhN2E5OGQyNzhmNDY1ZmYzZmEyZjlkOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/adhar-io/adhar-console/commit/37697429ede5865a212e797fbd06e4b8c44c8621","sha":"37697429ede5865a212e797fbd06e4b8c44c8621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/37697429ede5865a212e797fbd06e4b8c44c8621"}],"sha":"8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/8e1cd14f3907199fa7a98d278f465ff3fa2f9d94"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2254963?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tapas4java","id":2254963,"login":"tapas4java","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTQ5NjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tapas4java","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/commits/37697429ede5865a212e797fbd06e4b8c44c8621/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:33:59Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:33:59Z","email":"tapas.friends@gmail.com","name":"Tapas Jena"},"message":"fix(platform): Cloud Shell opens a terminal, and Logs actually stream\n\nTwo separate faults, each of which made its page useless.\n\nCloud Shell could not load its terminal runtime. The xterm stylesheet was a\nDYNAMIC `import(''…/xterm.css?inline'')`, so the browser fetched that URL\nitself and the dev server answered it as `text/css` — not a module — and the\nimport rejected with \"Failed to fetch dynamically imported module\". It sat in\nthe same `Promise.all` as the core terminal, so a stylesheet that could not\nbe parsed as JavaScript took the whole terminal down: every session showed\n\"Could not load the terminal runtime\". The stylesheet is now a static import,\nwhich the bundler transforms in dev and in a build alike, and a missing one\nfalls back to the handful of rules the terminal genuinely cannot work\nwithout — chiefly the off-screen helper textarea that xterm reads keystrokes\nfrom — rather than failing.\n\nLogs streamed nothing because the viewer passed the namespace FILTER to the\nstream instead of the pod''s own namespace. That filter is empty when it reads\n\"All namespaces\", which is its default, so the hook bailed to `idle` and\nnever requested a line: the page showed a pod, a container and a tail size,\nthen \"Waiting for log output…\" forever. Picking a pod is what names the\nnamespace; the filter only decides which pods are offered.\n\nVerified against the live cluster: a cluster shell accepts `echo` and the pod\nechoes it back, and selecting a running pod streams 74 lines.","tree":{"sha":"b983babfc6a89a46a5a34108e14fbeb0d8860aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/trees/b983babfc6a89a46a5a34108e14fbeb0d8860aa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/adhar-io/adhar-console/git/commits/37697429ede5865a212e797fbd06e4b8c44c8621","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}